/* 124 original applied cases. Source references locate topics; no official-exam calibration. */
const COVERAGE_MARKET_CREDIT=[{"id":"b001","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-1.2","reading":"MR-1","concept":"Lognormal loss quantile","question":"A EUR 20m equity holding has log return N(0.0004,0.02²) over one day. Use z0.01=−2.326 and loss=V(1−exp(r)). Its one-day 99% VaR is closest to:","choices":["EUR 0.938m","EUR 0.046m","EUR 0.400m","EUR 0.901m"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le quantile bas du rendement logarithmique vaut 0,0004−2,326×0,02=−0,04612. La perte est 20[1−exp(−0,04612)]≈0,901 M.","why":["Utilise une approximation linéaire avec une dérive mal signée.","Confond rendement logarithmique et montant en millions.","Ne prend qu’un écart-type.","Transforme le quantile logarithmique en perte monétaire."],"cue":"Quantile de log-return puis transformation exponentielle.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"20*(1-Math.exp(0.0004-2.326*0.02))","value":0.9014527193744226,"optionValue":0.901,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b002","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-1.5","reading":"MR-1","concept":"Sampling error at the tail","question":"Two independent historical VaR estimates use the same quantile and the same density near that quantile. One uses 400 daily observations; the other 1,600. Under the asymptotic quantile standard-error formula, the second standard error is:","choices":["0.5 times the first","2.0 times the first","1.0 times the first","0.25 times the first"],"answer":0,"explanation":"À densité et quantile identiques, SE est proportionnelle à 1/√n. Multiplier n par quatre divise SE par deux.","why":["Applique la racine carrée à la taille d’échantillon.","Inverse le sens de l’effet.","Ignore l’effet de la taille d’échantillon.","La variance est divisée par quatre, pas son écart-type."],"cue":"SE d’un quantile : effet en racine de n.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"Math.sqrt(400/1600)","value":0.5,"optionValue":0.5,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b003","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-1.6","reading":"MR-1","concept":"QQ evidence against normal tails","question":"A normal QQ plot places theoretical normal quantiles on the horizontal axis and standardized losses on the vertical axis. The lower end bends below the fitted line and the upper end bends above it. What is the strongest interpretation?","choices":["Both tails are lighter than those of the fitted normal distribution","Only the loss mean differs from the fitted normal mean","Both observed tails are heavier than the fitted normal tails","The curvature establishes serial dependence in returns"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les deux extrêmes s’écartent vers l’extérieur : les quantiles observés sont plus extrêmes que ceux de la normale ajustée.","why":["Les quantiles observés sont plus extrêmes, pas moins.","Un déplacement de moyenne produirait surtout un décalage, pas cette courbure bilatérale.","Lit correctement les deux queues.","Un QQ plot marginal ne teste pas la dépendance temporelle."],"cue":"Lire les axes avant de diagnostiquer les queues.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b004","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-2.1","reading":"MR-2","concept":"Bootstrap uncertainty versus new scenarios","question":"A desk repeatedly resamples 500 observed daily loss vectors with replacement and recalculates ES. Which conclusion is justified?","choices":["The bootstrap extrapolates crisis severities by multiplying the largest observed losses","Resampling each asset independently preserves the observed joint loss distribution","The procedure estimates sampling variability conditional on the empirical history","A narrow bootstrap interval establishes that the historical window is representative"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le bootstrap renseigne sur la variabilité d’échantillonnage sous la distribution empirique retenue ; il n’invente pas de nouvelles crises.","why":["Le bootstrap empirique ne multiplie pas les pertes pour extrapoler.","Le rééchantillonnage séparé détruit la dépendance contemporaine.","Distingue incertitude d’échantillonnage et risque de modèle.","L’incertitude conditionnelle ne prouve pas la représentativité."],"cue":"Bootstrap : incertitude autour de l’histoire, pas crise inconnue.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b005","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-2.2","reading":"MR-2","concept":"Kernel bandwidth trade-off","question":"A kernel estimator of the loss density produces a highly jagged tail when bandwidth is very small. Increasing bandwidth materially is most likely to:","choices":["Move every estimated tail quantile in a conservative direction","Reduce local variance but increase smoothing bias","Reduce smoothing bias while increasing local variance","Increase the number of independent tail realizations available for estimation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Une bande plus large lisse davantage : moins de bruit local, mais davantage de biais possible dans les détails et les queues.","why":["Le sens du biais sur les quantiles n’est pas garanti.","Décrit le compromis biais-variance.","Inverse l’effet du lissage.","L’historique sous-jacent ne gagne pas de nouvelles observations."],"cue":"Un lissage plus fort échange variance contre biais.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b006","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-2.4","reading":"MR-2","concept":"Unseen nonlinear exposure","question":"A desk launches a short digital-option book. Its historical simulation sample contains no move across the digital strike. Which limitation matters most?","choices":["Bootstrapping the same sample necessarily adds the missing strike-crossing states","Historical simulation can miss losses from states absent from its historical scenarios","Its only material limitation is failure to account for current volatility","Full nonlinear revaluation removes the need for a historical strike-crossing scenario"],"answer":1,"explanation":"La revalorisation peut traiter la non-linéarité, mais une histoire sans franchissement ne représente pas ce scénario.","why":["Le bootstrap répète le support empirique sans le garantir plus riche.","La richesse des scénarios limite le modèle.","Adapter la volatilité ne suffit pas à assurer la couverture du payoff discontinu.","La revalorisation ne crée pas un état absent."],"cue":"Une bonne revalorisation ne répare pas un scénario absent.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b007","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-3.1","reading":"MR-3","concept":"Rare-event data scarcity","question":"A risk manager fits a 99.99% daily loss quantile using 1,000 observations. Which concern is most material even if the fitted curve looks smooth?","choices":["The estimate is precise because the confidence level is far above the sample mean","The principal uncertainty disappears if the fitted tail density is continuous","Using all 1,000 observations as tail observations avoids any extrapolation assumption","Only about 0.1 observation is expected beyond that quantile, making the estimate heavily dependent on tail assumptions"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le nombre attendu de dépassements est 1000×0,0001=0,1. L’extrapolation extrême dépend donc fortement du modèle et de ses paramètres.","why":["Un niveau de confiance ne fournit pas de précision statistique.","La continuité ne garantit pas la bonne spécification.","Inclure le centre de distribution ne transforme pas ces points en observations extrêmes.","Quantifie la rareté de l’information."],"cue":"Compter les observations attendues dans la queue.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"1000*(1-0.9999)","value":0.09999999999998899,"optionValue":0.1,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b008","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-3.3","reading":"MR-3","concept":"Threshold choice in POT","question":"A POT fit uses nearly all observations as threshold exceedances. A validator proposes raising the threshold substantially. What is the central trade-off?","choices":["Less parameter variance because the exceedances are more extreme","Less asymptotic tail-model bias but greater parameter uncertainty from fewer exceedances","A lower threshold is always preferable because its fit uses more observations","Less tail-model bias and more threshold exceedances available for estimation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Un seuil plus élevé rapproche la modélisation des valeurs extrêmes, mais laisse moins de données pour estimer les paramètres.","why":["Moins de points augmente généralement l’incertitude d’estimation.","Décrit le compromis seuil-biais-variance.","La quantité de données ne supprime pas le biais de modèle.","Un seuil plus élevé laisse moins de dépassements."],"cue":"Seuil élevé : meilleure approximation, moins de données.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b009","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-3.6","reading":"MR-3","concept":"Joint tail dependence","question":"Two loss pairs have similar Pearson correlations. Pair A exhibits many joint extreme losses; pair B almost none. What should an extreme-risk analysis conclude?","choices":["Dependence in the joint tail must be modeled separately from ordinary linear correlation","Separate marginal EVT fits are sufficient to identify the joint extreme distribution","Pair A can be treated as safer because its common tail events are easier to observe","Similar Pearson correlations imply comparable extreme-loss diversification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Une corrélation résume une relation linéaire globale et ne détermine pas la dépendance des extrêmes.","why":["Cible la dépendance extrême.","Les marges ne déterminent pas la dépendance.","Une meilleure observabilité ne réduit pas le risque intrinsèque décrit.","Une corrélation commune n’identifie pas les queues jointes."],"cue":"Corrélation globale et dépendance de queue sont distinctes.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b010","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-4.1","reading":"MR-4","concept":"Clean comparison for a VaR backtest","question":"A one-day VaR forecast assumes unchanged positions, but actual daily P&L includes substantial intraday trading. Which comparison best isolates the modeled market-risk forecast?","choices":["Compare the current VaR with the previous week’s average actual P&L","Add all intraday trading P&L to the forecast VaR before counting exceptions","Remove intraday gains but retain intraday losses in the test P&L","Compare VaR with hypothetical P&L on the unchanged opening portfolio"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le P&L hypothétique à positions constantes rapproche le périmètre testé de celui du modèle de VaR.","why":["Le décalage temporel et le portefeuille ne correspondent plus.","Modifier le quantile avec un P&L réalisé n’est pas une prévision cohérente.","Un traitement asymétrique contamine le test.","Aligne le portefeuille et l’horizon."],"cue":"Backtest : même portefeuille, même horizon, même définition de perte.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b011","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-4.2","reading":"MR-4","concept":"Backtesting power at high confidence","question":"A 99.9% daily VaR model produces no exceptions over 250 days. What is the most defensible conclusion?","choices":["The model must be rejected because the expected exception count is not zero","The sample has little power to distinguish well-calibrated and moderately misspecified rare-event forecasts","The absence of VaR exceptions is sufficient evidence that tail-loss severity is accurate","No exceptions establishes that the model is conservatively calibrated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"On attend seulement 0,25 exception. Zéro dépassement ne suffit pas à établir une calibration précise à ce niveau.","why":["Le nombre attendu n’impose pas un nombre réalisé déterministe.","Reconnaît la faible puissance de l’échantillon.","La sévérité au-delà du quantile n’est pas identifiée.","Un non-rejet ne prouve pas une calibration prudente."],"cue":"Très haute confiance : très peu d’information dans les exceptions.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b012","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-4.4","reading":"MR-4","concept":"Type II error in model validation","question":"A validator tests the null that a VaR model is adequately calibrated. The model is materially underestimating risk, but the test fails to reject. This is:","choices":["A Type II error","Proof that the model is correct","A Type I error","An exception independence test"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Ne pas rejeter une hypothèse nulle fausse est une erreur de type II. Le risque est de conserver un modèle déficient.","why":["Identifie l’erreur de non-détection.","Un non-rejet ne prouve pas la nulle.","Le type I rejette une nulle vraie.","La nature de l’erreur ne précise pas le test employé."],"cue":"Type II : laisser passer un mauvais modèle.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b013","topic":"market","skill":"m-hedge","objective":"MR-5.2","reading":"MR-5","concept":"General and specific mapped risk","question":"A corporate-bond portfolio has independent general-rate and issuer-specific P&L components with standard deviations EUR 3m and EUR 4m. Assuming normality and z=2.33, combined VaR is:","choices":["EUR 11.65m","EUR 16.31m","EUR 7.00m","EUR 5.00m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les variances indépendantes s’additionnent : σ=√(3²+4²)=5. VaR=2,33×5=11,65 M.","why":["Agrège d’abord les variances puis applique z.","Suppose implicitement une corrélation parfaite positive.","Additionne des écarts-types sans le quantile.","Donne σ, pas la VaR."],"cue":"Risque général et spécifique : agréger avant le quantile.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"2.33*Math.sqrt(3*3+4*4)","value":11.65,"optionValue":11.65,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b014","topic":"market","skill":"m-hedge","objective":"MR-5.3","reading":"MR-5","concept":"Cash-flow mapping preserves curve exposure","question":"Two fixed-income portfolios have identical market value and duration but cash flows concentrated at very different maturities. Which mapping best distinguishes their exposure to a curve twist?","choices":["Map dated cash flows to multiple curve vertices","Map both portfolios to the same single duration-matched zero-coupon security","Map all interim cash flows to the final maturity while preserving total present value","Map both portfolios using only parallel DV01 and ignore payment dates"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Des sommets de courbe multiples préservent la localisation des flux et rendent visibles les mouvements non parallèles.","why":["Conserve la localisation des flux et le risque non parallèle.","Une seule sensibilité écrase les différences d’échéance.","Préserver la valeur ne préserve pas les sensibilités aux points de courbe.","La neutralité parallèle ne révèle pas le twist."],"cue":"Même duration ne signifie pas même risque de courbe.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b015","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-5.6","reading":"MR-5","concept":"Benchmark-relative risk","question":"A fund and its benchmark have return volatilities 12% and 10%, with correlation 0.95. Under a zero-mean normal active-return approximation, use z=2.33. One-year 99% active VaR as a percentage of NAV is closest to:","choices":["51.26%","27.96%","9.32%","4.00%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"σ actif=√(0,12²+0,10²−2×0,95×0,12×0,10)=4 %. VaR active=2,33×4 %=9,32 %.","why":["Additionne les volatilités.","Utilise la volatilité du fonds seul.","Calcule la variance de la différence.","Donne seulement l’écart-type actif."],"cue":"Risque relatif = risque du rendement fonds moins benchmark.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*2.33*Math.sqrt(.12**2+.10**2-2*.95*.12*.10)","value":9.320000000000002,"optionValue":9.32,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b016","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-6.1","reading":"MR-6","concept":"Conceptual validation of nonlinear risk","question":"A short-option desk uses delta-normal VaR, and the model passes a quiet-year exception test. Which finding most directly challenges conceptual soundness?","choices":["The model ignores gamma and volatility changes material to the desk under stress","The desk performs a separate realized-P&L reconciliation each day","The VaR uses current position sizes rather than last year’s average positions","The quiet sample has fewer exception observations than a crisis sample"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Un modèle linéaire peut manquer les principaux mécanismes de perte d’une position short options, même après un backtest calme.","why":["Cible l’inadéquation entre exposition et hypothèses.","Une réconciliation est utile et ne constitue pas une défaillance conceptuelle.","Les positions actuelles sont un choix approprié.","La rareté d’exceptions concerne la puissance du test, mais ne décrit pas directement l’omission conceptuelle."],"cue":"Valider d’abord les mécanismes de perte.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b017","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-6.2","reading":"MR-6","concept":"Sensitivity to tail-window assumptions","question":"A VaR estimate changes little when today’s prices are perturbed but doubles when an old crisis week enters the history window. What should validation prioritize?","choices":["Conclude the model is robust because the local price perturbations had little effect","Investigating window composition and sensitivity to influential tail scenarios","Average the two reported VaRs and treat the midpoint as a validated forecast","Increase the daily reporting frequency while leaving historical assumptions unexamined"],"answer":1,"explanation":"La robustesse dépend aussi du choix d’historique. Une semaine influente mérite analyse, justification et tests de sensibilité.","why":["La robustesse locale ne couvre pas l’historique.","Identifie le paramètre réellement influent.","Une moyenne de chiffres ne remplace pas la validation des hypothèses.","La fréquence du reporting ne traite pas la sensibilité observée."],"cue":"Tester les hypothèses de données autant que les prix.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b018","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-6.3","reading":"MR-6","concept":"Quantile uncertainty with clustered losses","question":"An analyst computes a VaR confidence interval assuming 1,000 independent returns, but large losses cluster during volatility regimes. What is the main issue?","choices":["The interval must become narrower because clustered tail losses repeat similar information","The confidence interval can be repaired simply by increasing the VaR confidence level","The nominal interval may be too narrow because independence overstates effective information","A conventional independent bootstrap automatically reproduces volatility regimes"],"answer":2,"explanation":"La dépendance réduit souvent l’information indépendante effective ; une méthode respectant cette dépendance est nécessaire.","why":["La répétition corrélée n’ajoute pas autant d’information indépendante.","Changer le quantile cible ne modélise pas la dépendance.","Explique la sous-estimation possible de l’incertitude.","Un bootstrap i.i.d. ne conserve pas cette dépendance."],"cue":"Un historique long peut contenir peu d’épisodes indépendants.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b019","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-7.1","reading":"MR-7","concept":"Uniform but serially dependent PITs","question":"A loss model generates PITs with an almost uniform histogram, yet high PITs strongly predict high PITs the next day. Which diagnosis is most appropriate?","choices":["Marginal calibration alone does not establish correct conditional forecasts","A uniform histogram proves that successive PITs are independent","The observed dependence can be ignored if average forecast losses are unbiased","Only the histogram matters because daily forecasts need no temporal conditioning"],"answer":0,"explanation":"L’uniformité marginale et l’indépendance sont deux propriétés distinctes. La prévisibilité des PIT révèle une structure non capturée.","why":["Sépare les deux exigences.","Une marge uniforme peut être dépendante dans le temps.","Une moyenne correcte n’élimine pas les erreurs de distribution conditionnelle.","La prévisibilité des PIT contredit des prévisions conditionnelles correctes."],"cue":"PIT : uniformité et indépendance.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b020","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-7.2","reading":"MR-7","concept":"Computing a PIT from a forecast CDF","question":"A continuous forecast loss CDF is F. The realized loss is EUR 2m and F(2)=0.92. The PIT and the forecast upper-tail probability beyond the realized loss are:","choices":["0.92 and 0.92","0.92 and 0.08","0.08 and 0.92","2.00 and 0.08"],"answer":1,"explanation":"PIT=F(L réalisé)=0,92 ; la probabilité prédite d’une perte plus grande vaut 1−0,92=0,08.","why":["Confond la masse cumulée et la queue.","Applique la définition et son complément.","Inverse CDF et queue.","Le PIT est une probabilité, pas un montant."],"cue":"PIT d’une perte = CDF prédite à la réalisation.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"1-.92","value":0.07999999999999996,"optionValue":0.08,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b021","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-7.4","reading":"MR-7","concept":"Choosing a tail-sensitive goodness-of-fit test","question":"PIT diagnostics suggest subtle deviations concentrated near 0 and 1. Relative to an unweighted integrated squared-distance test, which choice explicitly puts more weight near the boundaries?","choices":["Cramér-von Mises with a constant integration weight, because it specifically upweights the tails","Anderson-Darling","A mean-only PIT test, because matching the mean determines boundary calibration","Kolmogorov-Smirnov, because its distance is explicitly inverse-weighted by u(1−u)"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Anderson-Darling pondère les écarts par un facteur qui augmente près des extrémités de la CDF.","why":["Le poids constant ne privilégie pas spécialement les bornes.","Répond au besoin de sensibilité aux queues.","La moyenne ne détermine pas les queues de la distribution.","KS utilise le plus grand écart absolu, sans cette pondération explicite."],"cue":"Le choix du test détermine les écarts les plus visibles.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b022","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-8.3","reading":"MR-8","concept":"Quanto drift sign","question":"Use the stated quanto drift adjustment μquanto=μforeign−ρσassetσFX. Let μforeign=4%, ρ=0.5, σasset=20%, and σFX=10%, with compatible FX quotation and annual units. The adjusted drift is:","choices":["5%","3%","4%","−6%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"L’ajustement vaut 0,5×0,20×0,10=1 %. Le drift ajusté est 4−1=3 %.","why":["Ajoute l’ajustement au lieu de le soustraire.","Applique la convention explicitement donnée.","Ignore le terme de corrélation.","Mélange pourcentages et décimales."],"cue":"Quanto : fixer la cotation et le signe avant le calcul.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(.04-.5*.2*.1)","value":3,"optionValue":3,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b023","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-8.4","reading":"MR-8","concept":"Correlation swap settlement","question":"A swap pays N(ρrealized−K), with N=EUR 2m per unit correlation and K=0.35. Realized correlation is 0.20. The receiver of realized correlation receives:","choices":["EUR 300,000","EUR −300,000","EUR 700,000","EUR −150,000"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le règlement vaut 2 M×(0,20−0,35)=−0,30 M : le receveur du réalisé doit payer.","why":["Inverse le sens de la différence.","Applique le notionnel par unité de corrélation.","Ne calcule que la jambe fixe.","Oublie le facteur deux du notionnel."],"cue":"Unité de corrélation : 0,15, pas 15.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"2000000*(.20-.35)","value":-299999.99999999994,"optionValue":-300000,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b024","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-8.7","reading":"MR-8","concept":"Correlation concentration under stress","question":"A dealer books exposures to 30 funds with different names, but each fund uses the same leveraged volatility-target strategy. What is the most relevant concentration concern?","choices":["Common strategies affect operational risk but cannot create portfolio concentration","Separate fund administrators necessarily eliminate correlation between their strategies","Legal name count is enough to justify independent exposure limits","Common deleveraging triggers can create correlated selling and system-wide exposure"],"answer":3,"explanation":"La diversité juridique masque une stratégie commune pouvant synchroniser les ventes et amplifier les pertes.","why":["Des stratégies communes créent aussi des expositions de marché communes.","L’administration juridique ne sépare pas les décisions de portefeuille.","Le nombre de noms ne garantit pas des facteurs diversifiés.","Identifie la concentration économique."],"cue":"Diversifier les mécanismes, pas seulement les noms.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b025","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-9.1","reading":"MR-9","concept":"Correlation and crisis regimes","question":"An equity portfolio is optimized using calm-period correlations. In stress, correlations and their volatility rise. Which implication is most defensible?","choices":["Rising correlation volatility matters only to correlation-swap valuation","Diversification benefits estimated from calm data may be overstated in the stress regime","The calm-period covariance matrix remains valid if each asset’s volatility is updated separately","A higher average pairwise correlation leaves long-only portfolio variance unchanged if weights are fixed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Pour des expositions longues communes, une corrélation plus forte réduit généralement les gains de diversification ; l’instabilité ajoute de l’incertitude.","why":["L’incertitude de corrélation affecte aussi le risque de portefeuille.","Tient compte du changement de régime.","Mettre à jour les marges ne corrige pas la dépendance.","Les covariances entrent dans la variance même à poids constants."],"cue":"Stress : remettre en cause le gain de diversification.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b026","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-9.2","reading":"MR-9","concept":"Discrete correlation mean reversion","question":"A fitted quarterly correlation process is ρt+1=0.12+0.60ρt+εt+1. Under this AR(1) specification, its long-run mean and one-step autocorrelation are:","choices":["0.30 and 0.40","0.12 and 0.40","0.20 and 0.60","0.30 and 0.60"],"answer":3,"explanation":"La moyenne stationnaire vaut 0,12/(1−0,60)=0,30. L’autocorrélation à un pas est le coefficient 0,60.","why":["Confond autocorrélation et ajustement vers la moyenne.","Confond constante et moyenne et utilise la vitesse discrète.","Divise par le coefficient au lieu de son complément.","Résout correctement l’espérance stationnaire."],"cue":"AR(1) : moyenne a/(1−b), autocorrélation b.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":".12/(1-.60)","value":0.3,"optionValue":0.3,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b027","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-9.3","reading":"MR-9","concept":"Respecting correlation support","question":"A model fits a normal distribution directly to a volatile sample correlation centered near 0.9. Which issue should a validator raise first?","choices":["Changing the mean to zero fixes the support problem without changing distribution family","Using more observations guarantees that a nondegenerate normal fit is bounded","The model assigns positive probability to impossible correlations above 1","A mean below 1 is sufficient to ensure all simulated correlations remain admissible"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une corrélation appartient à [−1,1]. Une loi normale non dégénérée sur la corrélation brute ne respecte pas ce support.","why":["La normale reste non bornée quel que soit son centre.","Un grand échantillon ne change pas le support de la loi ajustée.","Identifie une incohérence de support.","Une moyenne admissible ne borne pas les réalisations."],"cue":"Le support est un premier contrôle du modèle.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b028","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-10.1","reading":"MR-10","concept":"Changing a copula with fixed marginals","question":"A portfolio model replaces a Gaussian copula with another dependence model while leaving each name’s default-time distribution unchanged. What can change?","choices":["Joint default probabilities and portfolio tail losses can change","The portfolio tail is determined solely by the unchanged marginal probabilities","Only expected single-name loss can change, while all joint events remain unchanged","Each obligor’s marginal default probability must change with the copula"],"answer":0,"explanation":"La copule relie les marges. La modifier peut changer les événements conjoints sans changer les probabilités marginales.","why":["Distingue marges et dépendance.","La dépendance est nécessaire pour construire la queue du portefeuille.","Les probabilités conjointes sont précisément concernées.","Les marges sont explicitement maintenues."],"cue":"Copule : relier les marges, pas les remplacer.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b029","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-10.2","reading":"MR-10","concept":"Independent Gaussian latent defaults","question":"Two obligors default when independent standard-normal latent variables fall below thresholds giving default probabilities 3% and 4%. Under this zero-correlation Gaussian copula, joint default probability is:","choices":["3.50%","7.00%","0.12%","12.00%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Avec indépendance, P(D1∩D2)=0,03×0,04=0,0012=0,12 %.","why":["Donne une moyenne de PD.","Additionne des probabilités.","Multiplie les probabilités indépendantes.","Convertit incorrectement le produit en pourcentage."],"cue":"Zéro corrélation gaussienne implique indépendance des latents.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*.03*.04","value":0.12,"optionValue":0.12,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b030","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-10.3","reading":"MR-10","concept":"Correlated default-time simulation","question":"A simulation produces correlated standard-normal draws Z_i for each obligor, transforms U_i=Φ(Z_i), and has cumulative default CDFs F_i(t). Which next step generates consistent default times?","choices":["Use one common deterministic default date for every draw","Discard F_i and rank only the Gaussian draws","Set τ_i=Z_i for all obligors","Set τ_i=F_i inverse(U_i)"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le changement Φ transforme les normales en uniformes dépendantes ; l’inverse de chaque CDF de défaut donne ensuite le temps de défaut.","why":["Détruit la structure marginale et aléatoire.","Les rangs seuls ne fixent pas les probabilités aux horizons.","Une normale n’est pas un temps de défaut.","Applique la transformation inverse avec la bonne marge."],"cue":"Latent normal → uniforme → temps de défaut.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b031","topic":"market","skill":"m-hedge","objective":"MR-11.1","reading":"MR-11","concept":"Residual basis in a DV01 hedge","question":"A corporate bond is hedged with government futures to make total parallel-rate DV01 zero. Which loss mechanism can still remain material?","choices":["Any infinitesimal parallel shift in the exact risk-free factor already neutralized","A fully predictable accounting accrual with no change in economic value","A coupon payment known at hedge inception, with no market or credit changes","A widening of the corporate credit spread with government yields unchanged"],"answer":3,"explanation":"La neutralité au taux parallèle ne neutralise pas le spread de crédit ni tous les mouvements de courbe ou de base.","why":["Ce facteur est celui neutralisé à l’ordre un.","L’accrual seul n’est pas le choc économique demandé.","Le paiement connu fait partie du cashflow prévu.","Identifie un facteur non couvert."],"cue":"Nommer le facteur que le hedge ne couvre pas.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b032","topic":"market","skill":"m-hedge","objective":"MR-11.6","reading":"MR-11","concept":"Levels regression versus changes","question":"Two yield series drift together in levels. A hedge ratio from a levels regression gives poor out-of-sample daily P&L hedging. What is the best next check?","choices":["Retain the levels hedge because levels R² is more important than realized hedge P&L","Select the hedge ratio that minimizes all in-sample losses without an independent test","Test whether level co-movement is spurious and estimate the relation in changes relevant to the hedge horizon","Use the reciprocal of the reverse-regression slope as a universal correction"],"answer":2,"explanation":"La relation entre niveaux peut être trompeuse. Le hedge quotidien dépend des variations et doit être évalué hors échantillon.","why":["Le R² de niveaux ne valide pas la couverture des variations.","Le surajustement ne constitue pas une preuve hors échantillon.","Aligne la régression sur les variations et vérifie les niveaux.","Les régressions inverses ne donnent pas généralement la même pente."],"cue":"Régression de hedge : horizon et variable de P&L pertinents.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b033","topic":"market","skill":"m-hedge","objective":"MR-11.7","reading":"MR-11","concept":"Reverse regression is not reciprocal","question":"Regressing changes in bond A on bond B gives βA|B=0.8 and R²=0.64. What is βB|A, given nonzero variances and standard OLS with an intercept?","choices":["0.512","1.25","0.64","0.80"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Les deux pentes ont pour produit ρ²=R². Donc βB|A=0,64/0,8=0,8 ; ce n’est pas 1/0,8.","why":["Multiplie au lieu de diviser.","La réciproque ne vaut que sous corrélation parfaite.","Confond R² et pente inverse.","Utilise le produit des deux pentes."],"cue":"Pentes inversées : leur produit vaut ρ².","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":".64/.8","value":0.7999999999999999,"optionValue":0.8,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b034","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-12.2","reading":"MR-12","concept":"Replicating a bond option","question":"At option expiry, a zero-coupon bond is worth 96 in the up state and 90 in the down state. A call strike is 92. The one-period risk-free growth factor is 1.02. Which bond units and cash today approximately replicate the call?","choices":["1.0000 bond units and cash −90.1961 today","0.6667 bond units and cash −58.8235 today","0.3333 bond units and cash −29.4118 today","0.6667 bond units and cash +58.8235 today"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les payoffs sont 4 et 0. Δ=(4−0)/(96−90)=2/3. Dans l’état bas : (2/3)×90+B×1,02=0, donc B=−60/1,02.","why":["Le payoff bas serait négatif.","Réplique exactement les deux états.","La pente est deux fois trop petite.","Le signe de l’emprunt est inversé."],"cue":"Répliquer les deux états avant de chercher une probabilité.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"(96-92)/(96-90)","value":0.6666666666666666,"optionValue":0.6667,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b035","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-12.6","reading":"MR-12","concept":"What an OAS removes","question":"Two callable bonds have the same observed yield spread but different embedded call-option values. A risk manager wants to compare residual spread compensation after modeling the call feature. Which metric is designed for this purpose?","choices":["Raw yield-to-maturity spread without modeling exercise","Coupon spread relative to the risk-free short rate","Option-adjusted spread from a consistent rate-tree valuation","Yield spread calculated using the first possible call date as a certain maturity"],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’OAS est le spread ajouté aux taux d’actualisation du modèle pour retrouver le prix après prise en compte de l’option.","why":["Le spread brut mélange optionalité et compensation résiduelle.","Le coupon seul n’isole pas la prime implicite dans le prix.","Ajuste explicitement l’optionalité modélisée.","Rendre l’exercice certain ne valorise pas son caractère conditionnel."],"cue":"OAS : spread résiduel conditionnel au modèle d’option.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b036","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-12.9","reading":"MR-12","concept":"Time-step refinement and convergence","question":"A short-rate tree is used to value a Bermudan option. Halving each time step changes the price substantially. Which response is best?","choices":["Use the midpoint of the two prices without further convergence checks","Accept the finer price as exact because doubling the number of steps eliminates model bias","Keep the coarse price because fewer steps reduce the number of numerical assumptions","Check convergence, exercise-date alignment and model calibration before treating the finer-tree result as reliable"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Un pas plus fin peut réduire l’erreur de discrétisation mais ne garantit ni convergence ni bonne représentation des dates ou de la calibration.","why":["Une moyenne ne prouve pas la convergence.","Le raffinement ne supprime pas le risque de modèle ni toutes les erreurs.","Un arbre grossier peut mal discrétiser l’exercice et les dynamiques.","Teste les sources numériques et de construction."],"cue":"Raffinement : vérifier la convergence, pas compter les nœuds.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b037","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-13.1","reading":"MR-13","concept":"Upward curve without pure rate expectations","question":"A forward rate exceeds the market’s physical expectation of the future short rate. What can reconcile this without an arbitrage?","choices":["Risk-neutral and physical expectations are identical whenever rates have a finite mean","The discrepancy proves an arbitrage between every spot bond and a forward contract","A term risk premium separates the forward rate from the physical expectation","The forward must be an unbiased physical forecast whenever bonds are default-free"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les forwards sont liés aux prix et à une mesure de valorisation ; une prime de risque peut les distinguer des anticipations physiques.","why":["La finitude de la moyenne ne rend pas les mesures identiques.","L’absence d’arbitrage porte sur les prix, pas sur une égalité imposée avec l’anticipation physique.","Reconnaît la compensation du risque.","L’absence de défaut n’efface pas la prime de taux."],"cue":"Forward n’est pas prévision physique pure.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b038","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-13.2","reading":"MR-13","concept":"Volatility and term-structure convexity","question":"Under risk-neutral pricing, a future one-year discount factor is exp(−r). Its mean rate remains fixed while normally distributed rate uncertainty increases. What happens to E[exp(−r)]?","choices":["It becomes negative","It rises because the discount factor is convex in r","It remains unchanged for every distribution","It falls because all uncertainty reduces prices"],"answer":1,"explanation":"L’exponentielle exp(−r) est convexe ; pour une normale de moyenne fixée, E[exp(−r)]=exp(−μ+σ²/2) augmente avec la variance.","why":["Un facteur exponentiel est positif.","Applique la convexité au bon objet.","La non-linéarité rend la variance pertinente.","Le signe dépend de la fonction, pas d’une règle générale."],"cue":"La volatilité agit via la convexité de l’actualisation.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b039","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-13.4","reading":"MR-13","concept":"Bond return decomposition","question":"Over one year, a bond is expected to earn 3% coupon carry, 0.8% roll-down, and lose 1.5% from the forecast curve shift. Ignoring convexity and reinvestment effects, expected total return is:","choices":["0.7%","3.8%","2.3%","5.3%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le rendement anticipé additionne les composantes signées : 3+0,8−1,5=2,3 %.","why":["Soustrait le roll-down au lieu de l’ajouter.","Ignore la perte anticipée de taux.","Additionne les contributions avec leurs signes.","Transforme la perte en gain."],"cue":"Décomposer carry, roll-down et variation de prix.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"3+.8-1.5","value":2.3,"optionValue":2.3,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b040","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-14.2","reading":"MR-14","concept":"Normal short-rate increment units","question":"A no-drift model is dr=σdW with σ=120 bp per square-root year. Over one month, use Δt=1/12. The standard deviation of the rate change is closest to:","choices":["120.0 bp","415.7 bp","10.0 bp","34.6 bp"],"answer":3,"explanation":"L’écart-type vaut σ√Δt=120√(1/12)=34,6 pb.","why":["Ignore la durée du pas.","Divise par la racine au lieu de multiplier.","Multiplie par Δt au lieu de sa racine.","Respecte les unités de diffusion."],"cue":"Diffusion : écart-type en racine du temps.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"120*Math.sqrt(1/12)","value":34.64101615137754,"optionValue":34.6,"tolerance":0.05}},{"id":"b041","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-14.5","reading":"MR-14","concept":"Fitting today is not predicting tomorrow","question":"An arbitrage-free interest-rate model is calibrated exactly to today’s zero-coupon prices. Which statement follows?","choices":["Exact initial-curve calibration establishes that its future physical rate forecasts are unbiased","The model reproduces those calibration instruments today but can still misprice options if volatility dynamics are unsuitable","The exact fit is sufficient to validate every exercise strategy in a Bermudan option","All volatility assumptions become irrelevant once zero-coupon prices are fitted"],"answer":1,"explanation":"L’ajustement de la courbe initiale ne suffit pas à déterminer les dynamiques ou les prix d’options.","why":["La mesure physique et les prévisions restent à valider.","Délimite ce que le fit établit.","Les décisions d’exercice dépendent des valeurs conditionnelles futures.","Les options dépendent de la dynamique de volatilité."],"cue":"Fit de courbe et validation de dynamique sont distincts.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b042","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-14.7","reading":"MR-14","concept":"Vasicek horizon and half-life","question":"For dr=0.5(0.04−r)dt+σdW and r0=0.02, expected r after two years and mean-reversion half-life are closest to:","choices":["3.26% and 0.50 years","4.00% and 2.00 years","2.74% and 0.69 years","3.26% and 1.39 years"],"answer":3,"explanation":"E[r2]=0,04+(0,02−0,04)e^(−1)=3,264 %. Demi-vie=ln(2)/0,5=1,386 an.","why":["Confond vitesse et demi-vie.","La moyenne cible n’est pas atteinte en temps fini.","Mauvais exposant et mauvaise demi-vie.","Applique les deux formules de mean reversion."],"cue":"Vasicek : écart résiduel exponentiel, demi-vie ln2/a.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(.04+(.02-.04)*Math.exp(-.5*2))","value":3.2642411176571158,"optionValue":3.26,"tolerance":0.01}},{"id":"b043","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-15.2","reading":"MR-15","concept":"Integrating deterministic volatility","question":"In dr=σ(t)dW with no drift, annual σ is 1% for the first half-year and 2% for the second half-year. Independent Brownian increments apply. One-year standard deviation is closest to:","choices":["1.50%","1.00%","1.58%","3.00%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Variance=0,01²×0,5+0,02²×0,5=0,00025. Racine=1,581 %.","why":["Moyenne les écarts-types au lieu des variances.","Ignore le second régime.","Intègre la variance sur les deux périodes.","Additionne les volatilités."],"cue":"Volatilité variable : intégrer σ² dt.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*Math.sqrt(.01**2*.5+.02**2*.5)","value":1.5811388300841895,"optionValue":1.58,"tolerance":0.01}},{"id":"b044","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-15.4","reading":"MR-15","concept":"CIR versus Gaussian behavior near zero","question":"A bank needs a rate model whose diffusion volatility decreases toward zero as the short rate approaches zero from above. Which specification has that feature?","choices":["dr=a(b−r)dt+σ√r dW","dr=a(b−r)dt+σ/√r dW","dr=μdt+σ(t)dW with volatility depending on calendar time alone","dr=a(b−r)dt+σdW"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Dans CIR, la volatilité instantanée est σ√r et baisse quand r tend vers zéro. Les conditions de frontière doivent aussi être examinées.","why":["Identifie la diffusion CIR dépendant du niveau.","L’inverse de la racine augmente près de zéro au lieu de diminuer.","Une volatilité déterministe ne baisse pas nécessairement avec r.","La diffusion de Vasicek reste constante."],"cue":"CIR : volatilité proportionnelle à √r.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b045","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-15.5","reading":"MR-15","concept":"Lognormal basis-point volatility","question":"For dr=μr dt+σr dW, σ=25% per square-root year. If the short rate rises from 2% to 4%, how does instantaneous annualized absolute volatility change?","choices":["From 100 bp to 50 bp","From 50 bp to 100 bp","From 25 bp to 25 bp","From 2 bp to 4 bp"],"answer":1,"explanation":"La volatilité absolue est σr. À 2 % : 0,25×0,02=0,005=50 pb ; à 4 % : 100 pb.","why":["Inverse l’effet du niveau.","Multiplie la volatilité relative par le niveau du taux.","Confond volatilité relative et absolue.","Omet le facteur de volatilité."],"cue":"Lognormal : volatilité relative fixe, volatilité en pb variable.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"10000*.25*.04","value":100,"optionValue":100,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b046","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-16.1","reading":"MR-16","concept":"Why multiple rate factors help","question":"A one-factor Gaussian short-rate model cannot reproduce independent changes in the level and curvature of an observed yield curve. What is a key motivation for a multi-factor Gauss+ structure?","choices":["Guarantee nonnegative rates by specifying all factors as Gaussian","Keep one shock but increase its scale until all yield-curve shapes fit simultaneously","Replace maturity-dependent factor loadings with a single identical loading for every tenor","Allow distinct rate factors and mean-reversion channels rather than forcing every move onto one shock"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Plusieurs facteurs enrichissent les formes de mouvements de courbe et leurs horizons ; le caractère gaussien ne garantit pas la positivité.","why":["Les facteurs gaussiens peuvent prendre des valeurs négatives.","Une échelle plus grande ne crée pas de nouvelles directions indépendantes.","Une sensibilité identique impose encore un mouvement trop restreint.","Décrit l’intérêt multifactoriel."],"cue":"Multifacteur : plusieurs formes et horizons de mouvement.","source":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/9781119835622.ch9","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b047","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-16.2","reading":"MR-16","concept":"Stochastic mean-reversion target","question":"In a specified Gauss+ cascade, the short rate reverts toward a medium factor, which reverts toward a long factor. Compared with a one-factor Vasicek model with a fixed long-run target, what is added?","choices":["The target toward which the short rate moves can itself evolve with other state variables","The model imposes one fixed target shared unchanged by every factor","The short rate ceases to mean-revert whenever the long factor changes","Every yield-curve movement can still be summarized by a single scalar loading"],"answer":0,"explanation":"La cible du taux court est un facteur évolutif, lui-même relié à une cible plus longue, au lieu d’une constante unique.","why":["Identifie le changement de dynamique.","La cascade contient des cibles distinctes et évolutives.","La cible peut changer tout en conservant le retour vers elle.","Plusieurs facteurs donnent une structure de mouvements plus riche."],"cue":"Gauss+ : la cible de retour peut elle-même bouger.","source":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/9781119835622.ch9","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b048","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-16.3","reading":"MR-16","concept":"Cascade drift calculation","question":"For this Gauss+ step, use dr=ar(m−r)dt, dm=am(l−m)dt+σm dWm, and dl=σl dWl. Let r=2%, m=3%, l=4%, ar=2, am=0.5, dt=0.25 and both Brownian increments zero. The short and medium rate changes are:","choices":["+200 bp and +50 bp","+25 bp and +50 bp","+12.5 bp and +50 bp","+50 bp and +12.5 bp"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Δr=2×(0,03−0,02)×0,25=0,005=50 pb. Δm=0,5×(0,04−0,03)×0,25=0,00125=12,5 pb.","why":["Omet le pas de temps.","Mélange vitesses et facteurs.","Intervertit les deux variations.","Applique chaque vitesse et chaque écart au bon facteur."],"cue":"Cascade : calculer chaque drift avec sa cible propre.","source":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/9781119835622.ch9","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"10000*2*(.03-.02)*.25","value":49.99999999999999,"optionValue":50,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b049","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-17.3","reading":"MR-17","concept":"Equity downside skew and loss tails","question":"Far-out-of-the-money equity puts trade at higher implied volatility than at-the-money options of the same maturity. Relative to a flat-volatility lognormal benchmark, what does this most naturally indicate?","choices":["Only expected physical returns have changed; the implied loss-tail shape is unchanged","The same volatility difference directly measures the physical probability of a crash","Downside states are priced more richly, consistent with a heavier risk-neutral left tail","The smile shows that call and put implied volatilities must differ at the same strike"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le skew traduit un prix relatif élevé des états baissiers sous la distribution implicite, sans identifier à lui seul les probabilités physiques.","why":["Un skew renseigne sur la forme implicite, pas seulement une moyenne physique.","Confond mesure de valorisation et probabilité physique.","Lie prix des puts et queue implicite.","La parité impose une cohérence call-put de même strike et échéance."],"cue":"Skew : information sur la queue implicite, pas PD physique.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b050","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-17.4","reading":"MR-17","concept":"FX quotation and symmetric tail concerns","question":"An FX dealer sees high implied volatilities for both low-strike and high-strike options relative to ATM. Which interpretation is most consistent?","choices":["Only the lower-strike tail is priced differently because FX options cannot price upper-tail risk","The higher wing volatilities establish a larger physical probability without any role for risk premia","Both large appreciation and depreciation states are priced more richly than under a flat-volatility benchmark","The smile uniquely identifies a symmetric normal distribution of future spot levels"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un smile élevé aux deux ailes reflète des prix relativement élevés pour les deux extrêmes par rapport au modèle à volatilité constante.","why":["Les deux extrêmes interviennent dans les payoffs FX.","Les prix implicites ne sont pas directement des fréquences physiques.","Interprète les deux ailes.","Un smile ne justifie pas une loi normale symétrique des niveaux."],"cue":"Smile FX : regarder les deux sens de variation.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b051","topic":"market","skill":"m-rates","objective":"MR-17.9","reading":"MR-17","concept":"A jump creates a discrete tail scenario","question":"A short-maturity equity option model adds a small probability of a large downward jump while holding the forward price fixed through a compensating drift adjustment. Which relative pricing effect is most plausible?","choices":["Compensating the drift makes tail-sensitive option payoffs insensitive to the jump","Only the ATM option can change because it is the only payoff exposed to the forward","Preserving the forward preserves the entire implied-volatility curve","OTM downside puts become richer relative to a no-jump diffusion benchmark"],"answer":3,"explanation":"La masse ajoutée dans un état de baisse extrême affecte fortement les payoffs convexes des puts OTM ; préserver le forward ne préserve pas chaque option.","why":["La compensation de moyenne n’annule pas le changement de queue.","Les options de différents strikes dépendent de parties différentes de la distribution.","Une moyenne fixée ne fixe pas tous les payoffs convexes.","Identifie le payoff sensible à la queue gauche."],"cue":"Même forward ne signifie pas mêmes prix d’options.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b052","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-18.1","reading":"MR-18","concept":"Tail severity in the FRTB rationale","question":"Two trading books have equal 99% VaR but very different average losses beyond their respective quantiles. Which FRTB-related change directly addresses this limitation of a quantile-only measure?","choices":["Use exception counts alone as a measure of loss magnitude","Use expected shortfall to measure average losses in the tail","Keep the same VaR percentile and replace stressed data with only recent calm data","Use median loss because it is less sensitive to outliers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"ES considère la sévérité moyenne au-delà du seuil, là où une VaR isolée ne décrit que la frontière de queue.","why":["Le nombre de dépassements ne décrit pas leur taille.","Cible la sévérité au-delà du quantile.","La calibration calme peut masquer le stress et ne mesure pas la sévérité.","La médiane exclut précisément l’extrême risque concerné."],"cue":"VaR localise la queue ; ES mesure sa sévérité.","source":"https://www.bis.org/committees/bcbs/basel-framework/standard/mar","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b053","topic":"market","skill":"m-tail","objective":"MR-18.2","reading":"MR-18","concept":"Single-bucket horizon scaling","question":"For a simplified isolated risk factor, assume independent stationary daily increments and square-root-of-time ES scaling. Ten-day ES is EUR 5m and the assigned liquidity horizon is 40 days. Scaled ES is:","choices":["EUR 40m","EUR 10m","EUR 20m","EUR 5m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Sous les hypothèses de ce cas isolé, ES40=5√(40/10)=10 M. L’agrégation FRTB complète emploie une structure plus détaillée.","why":["Multiplie sans ratio cohérent.","Applique la racine du ratio des horizons.","Utilise un scaling linéaire.","Ignore le changement d’horizon."],"cue":"Pour un facteur isolé : préciser l’hypothèse de scaling.","source":"https://www.bis.org/committees/bcbs/basel-framework/standard/mar/33/inforce/2023-01-01/published/2020-06-05","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"5*Math.sqrt(40/10)","value":10,"optionValue":10,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b054","topic":"market","skill":"m-valid","objective":"MR-18.3","reading":"MR-18","concept":"P&L attribution eligibility","question":"A trading desk passes a VaR exception backtest but its risk-theoretical P&L persistently fails to explain hypothetical P&L because material risk factors are omitted. What is the relevant FRTB lesson?","choices":["Backtesting alone is sufficient for internal-model eligibility","P&L attribution addresses risk representation and can restrict internal-model use despite acceptable exception frequency","Omitted factors are irrelevant if average P&L is positive","Moving positions between books automatically resolves model eligibility"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le test PLA évalue si le modèle de risque représente suffisamment les facteurs expliquant le P&L. Il répond à une question différente du décompte d’exceptions.","why":["Les deux dispositifs ont des exigences distinctes.","Identifie le risque de représentation manquante.","La rentabilité moyenne ne valide pas le modèle.","Le transfert de portefeuille n’est pas une correction automatique."],"cue":"Exceptions et attribution P&L contrôlent deux angles.","source":"https://www.bis.org/committees/bcbs/basel-framework/standard/mar/32/inforce/2023-01-01/published/2020-03-27","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b055","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-1.1","reading":"CR-1","concept":"Credit risk before an actual missed payment","question":"A bank holds a fixed-rate corporate bond. Risk-free yields are unchanged, but deteriorating borrower quality widens its credit spread and lowers the bond price. Which conclusion is correct?","choices":["The loss must equal the expected principal loss conditional on immediate default","Credit deterioration can create a mark-to-market credit loss before default","The loss is market risk only because no contractual payment has been missed","The bond’s fixed coupon means only risk-free duration can explain a price change"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le risque de crédit inclut la détérioration de qualité et l’élargissement du spread, avant tout défaut réalisé.","why":["Un mouvement de prix n’est pas égal par définition à LGD.","Reconnaît la migration et le spread.","Le spread peut refléter un risque de crédit avant défaut.","Un coupon fixe laisse subsister le risque de spread et de défaut."],"cue":"Crédit : perte de valeur avant défaut possible.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b056","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-1.2","reading":"CR-1","concept":"Solvency versus contractual default","question":"A firm has assets with a sound going-concern value above liabilities but cannot make a contractual payment due today and has not entered court proceedings. Which statement is most precise?","choices":["The absence of court proceedings means there can be liquidity stress but no default","The missed payment proves that formal bankruptcy proceedings have already begun","Its positive asset surplus rules out contractual default until liabilities exceed assets","It can be in contractual default without proven balance-sheet insolvency or a formal bankruptcy filing"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Un défaut porte sur une obligation contractuelle ; l’insolvabilité et la procédure juridique sont des notions distinctes.","why":["Le défaut contractuel n’exige pas une procédure de faillite.","Une procédure juridique n’est pas automatiquement déclenchée au même instant.","Des actifs illiquides peuvent empêcher un paiement exigible.","Distingue les trois notions."],"cue":"Défaut contractuel, insolvabilité, faillite : trois diagnostics.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b057","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-1.3","reading":"CR-1","concept":"Undrawn commitment exposure","question":"A bank gives a borrower an irrevocable EUR 40m line, of which EUR 10m is drawn. The borrower tends to draw additional funds when credit quality deteriorates. Which exposure assessment is most appropriate?","choices":["Subtract all future commitment fees from the contractual line before measuring exposure","Consider current drawings plus plausible additional drawings before default","Use EUR 40m times current PD as the exposure at default","Use only EUR 10m because EAD excludes all off-balance-sheet commitments"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Une ligne engagée peut être tirée avant le défaut ; l’EAD doit considérer les engagements hors bilan et leur comportement en stress.","why":["Les commissions ne sont pas automatiquement des garanties disponibles au défaut.","Tient compte du mécanisme de conversion.","EAD ne se confond pas avec une perte attendue pondérée par PD.","Ignore les tirages futurs engagés."],"cue":"Engagement non tiré : exposition potentielle, pas zéro risque.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b058","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-1.5","reading":"CR-1","concept":"Taking credit risk for compensated return","question":"A lender can earn a 5% spread on a highly concentrated borrower exposure. Management argues that a positive spread alone justifies the loan. Which response is strongest?","choices":["Compare the contractual spread with the hurdle rate without adjusting for the capital base","Assess expected losses, operating and funding costs, concentration and capital consumption before concluding that the spread compensates risk","Compare the spread only with expected loss because unexpected losses are diversified even in a concentrated book","Accept if the borrower’s PD is below the portfolio average, regardless of LGD and concentration"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le spread brut doit couvrir les pertes attendues, les coûts et la rémunération du capital et du risque de concentration.","why":["Un spread sur EAD et un rendement sur capital n’ont pas le même dénominateur.","Relie le risque et la rémunération nette.","La concentration limite la diversification du risque inattendu.","Une PD seule ne mesure ni sévérité ni consommation de capital."],"cue":"Spread positif ne suffit pas : mesurer la rémunération nette du risque.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b059","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-2.1","reading":"CR-2","concept":"Independent credit assurance","question":"A business unit originates loans, an independent credit-risk function challenges approval assumptions, and internal audit assesses whether the framework works. Which change most undermines this arrangement?","choices":["Give the credit-risk function access to current borrower files and exceptions","Require the origination team alone to certify the effectiveness of independent oversight","Require the risk function to challenge borrower cash-flow assumptions before approval","Let internal audit report material framework failures to the board committee"],"answer":1,"explanation":"L’auto-certification par l’équipe qui prend le risque ne remplace pas une assurance indépendante sur les contrôles.","why":["L’accès aux informations favorise l’exercice du contrôle.","Remplace l’assurance indépendante par l’auto-certification.","Le challenge avant décision soutient la séparation des rôles.","Une escalade indépendante est appropriée."],"cue":"L’assurance indépendante ne se délègue pas à l’origination.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b060","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-2.3","reading":"CR-2","concept":"Limits without expertise","question":"A bank introduces a complex collateralized lending product and gives the desk a formal exposure limit. No approver understands the collateral liquidation assumptions. Which governance weakness remains?","choices":["Risk knowledge is unnecessary if the collateral has a published market price","A limit does not replace the skills needed to evaluate and oversee the product","The limit is sufficient if it is expressed as a percentage of total bank capital","The product can be treated as understood once the legal documentation is standardized"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les limites encadrent une prise de risque qui doit rester comprise, évaluée et surveillée par des personnes compétentes.","why":["La liquidité et le mécanisme de liquidation doivent être compris.","Identifie le manque de capacité d’analyse.","Un dénominateur prudent ne garantit pas que la limite est bien calibrée.","La standardisation juridique ne prouve pas la compréhension économique."],"cue":"Guidelines, compétences, limites et supervision sont complémentaires.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b061","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-2.5","reading":"CR-2","concept":"Credit committee escalation","question":"A proposed facility is profitable but would breach the approved sector concentration limit. The relationship manager asks the credit committee to approve silently because borrower PD is low. What is best?","choices":["Apply the formal exception and escalation process, assess aggregate concentration and document the decision","Treat high expected revenue as authority to exceed a board-approved limit without escalation","Approve using borrower PD alone because a low PD dominates all concentration measures","Reclassify the facility into a different sector to preserve apparent limit compliance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le comité doit traiter le dépassement selon les délégations et apprécier le portefeuille, pas seulement le nom isolé.","why":["Respecte la gouvernance et le portefeuille.","La rémunération ne remplace pas la délégation et la décision formelle.","Un portefeuille de faibles PD peut rester concentré.","Le changement d’étiquette ne modifie pas l’exposition économique."],"cue":"Une exception doit être justifiée, autorisée et traçable.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b062","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-3.4","reading":"CR-3","concept":"Classification after temporary payment relief","question":"A bank grants a stressed borrower six months of payment deferral. The borrower has weak projected cash flows and can repay only if a highly uncertain asset sale occurs. Which classification approach is most defensible?","choices":["Use collateral book value as a full substitute for forward repayment analysis","Restore the performing classification because no payment is due during the deferral period","Assess repayment capacity and the economic deterioration rather than treating the deferral as proof of recovery","Restore the original rating because extending maturity removes the near-term maturity wall"],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’aménagement du calendrier ne démontre pas le rétablissement de la capacité de remboursement ; il faut analyser la situation économique.","why":["Une valeur comptable ne garantit pas la réalisation ni les flux.","Le calendrier ne prouve pas la capacité économique.","S’appuie sur la substance du risque.","Un report de remboursement ne rétablit pas à lui seul la qualité de crédit."],"cue":"Un rééchelonnement ne crée pas la capacité de paiement.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b063","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-3.7","reading":"CR-3","concept":"IFRS 9 deterioration without default","question":"A loan’s credit risk has increased significantly since initial recognition, but it is not credit-impaired. Under the standard IFRS 9 staging approach, which ECL horizon is generally relevant?","choices":["Only losses on defaults already incurred","Lifetime ECL","Always exactly twelve months of cash shortfalls","No allowance until a missed payment"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Une augmentation significative du risque de crédit conduit généralement au stade 2 et aux pertes de crédit attendues à vie, sans nécessiter un défaut.","why":["L’approche est prospective.","Applique le principe du stade 2.","Le 12-month ECL n’est pas douze mois de seuls cash shortfalls.","Attendre le défaut contredit le mécanisme ECL."],"cue":"SICR : horizon de défaut à vie, pas attente du défaut.","source":"https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ifrs-9-financial-instruments/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b064","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-3.8","reading":"CR-3","concept":"Workout choice on discounted recoveries","question":"A distressed loan can be sold immediately for EUR 5.8m or retained for an expected EUR 7.0m recovery in two years, with EUR 0.4m workout cost paid today. Use a 10% annual discount rate and ignore all other effects. Which has the larger expected NPV?","choices":["Retain, because retention NPV is EUR 6.60m","Sell, because retention NPV is about EUR 5.39m","Retain, because 7.0 exceeds 5.8","They are equal by definition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"NPV de conservation=7/1,1²−0,4≈5,385 M, inférieur au prix immédiat de 5,8 M.","why":["Ignore l’actualisation.","Actualise puis déduit le coût immédiat.","Compare des montants à des dates différentes.","Aucune identité n’impose l’égalité."],"cue":"Workout : comparer les cashflows actualisés nets.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"7/(1.1**2)-.4","value":5.385123966942148,"optionValue":5.39,"tolerance":0.01}},{"id":"b065","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-4.4","reading":"CR-4","concept":"Single-name unexpected loss","question":"A one-year loan has fixed EAD EUR 8m, deterministic LGD 50%, and Bernoulli default probability 4%. Define UL as the standard deviation of credit loss. UL is closest to:","choices":["EUR 1.600m","EUR 4.000m","EUR 0.784m","EUR 0.160m"],"answer":2,"explanation":"UL=EAD×LGD×√[p(1−p)]=8×0,5×√(0,04×0,96)≈0,784 M.","why":["Omet le facteur de survie et mélange les unités.","C’est la perte conditionnelle au défaut.","Calcule l’écart-type de la variable de perte.","C’est la perte attendue."],"cue":"UL n’est pas EL : partir de la variance de perte.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"8*.5*Math.sqrt(.04*.96)","value":0.7838367176906169,"optionValue":0.784,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b066","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-4.5","reading":"CR-4","concept":"Default-rate estimation variability","question":"A homogeneous pool has 2,000 independent obligors with one-year PD 2%. What is the standard deviation of the realized portfolio default RATE?","choices":["6.261 percentage points","0.313 percentage points","28.000 percentage points","1.980 percentage points"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Var(taux)=p(1−p)/n=0,02×0,98/2000. Racine=0,0031305, soit 0,313 point de pourcentage.","why":["Utilise le nombre de défauts sans normalisation.","Normalise le nombre de défauts par n.","Ignore la taille du portefeuille.","Confond dispersion du taux et niveau de PD."],"cue":"Variance du taux binomial = p(1−p)/n.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*Math.sqrt(.02*.98/2000)","value":0.31304951684997057,"optionValue":0.313,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b067","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-4.6","reading":"CR-4","concept":"Diversification of loss volatility","question":"Two credit assets have loss standard deviations EUR 3m and EUR 4m and loss correlation 0.25. Portfolio UL, defined as loss standard deviation, is closest to:","choices":["EUR 5.57m","EUR 31.00m","EUR 5.00m","EUR 7.00m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Variance=3²+4²+2×0,25×3×4=31. UL=√31≈5,57 M.","why":["Inclut la covariance des pertes.","Confond variance et écart-type.","Suppose une corrélation nulle.","Suppose corrélation parfaite."],"cue":"Additionner variances et covariances avant la racine.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"Math.sqrt(3**2+4**2+2*.25*3*4)","value":5.5677643628300215,"optionValue":5.57,"tolerance":0.01}},{"id":"b068","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-5.1","reading":"CR-5","concept":"CAMEL trade-off","question":"A bank reports rapid earnings growth funded by short-term wholesale borrowing, while liquid assets shrink and delinquent loans rise. Which assessment best fits a CAMEL review?","choices":["Rising delinquency is irrelevant until all impaired loans have been written off","Liquidity can be excluded if the bank meets a minimum capital ratio","Earnings strength must be assessed alongside asset quality, liquidity, capital and management risks","Higher earnings outweigh deteriorating asset quality because profits are recognized first"],"answer":2,"explanation":"CAMEL organise plusieurs dimensions : capital, qualité d’actifs, management, rentabilité et liquidité. Une dimension ne suffit pas.","why":["La qualité d’actifs doit être analysée avant la perte définitive.","Solvabilité réglementaire et liquidité sont différentes.","Réconcilie les différentes dimensions.","La rentabilité peut être temporaire et ne compense pas automatiquement tous les risques."],"cue":"CAMEL : ne pas confondre rentabilité et solidité globale.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b069","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-5.3","reading":"CR-5","concept":"Capital ratio after asset risk weighting","question":"A bank holds EUR 100m of loans weighted 100% and EUR 50m of exposures weighted 20%. Eligible capital is EUR 14m. Ignoring other assets and capital adjustments, its capital-to-RWA ratio is:","choices":["28.00%","14.00%","9.33%","12.73%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"RWA=100+50×0,20=110 M. Ratio=14/110=12,73 %.","why":["Utilise uniquement la seconde exposition.","Omet les actifs pondérés à 20 %.","Utilise l’actif brut comme dénominateur.","Calcule les RWA puis le ratio."],"cue":"Ratio réglementaire : capital sur RWA, pas sur actif brut.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*14/(100+50*.2)","value":12.727272727272727,"optionValue":12.73,"tolerance":0.01}},{"id":"b070","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-5.7","reading":"CR-5","concept":"Loan RAROC after expected loss","question":"A loan produces EUR 2.4m revenue, EUR 0.8m funding and operating costs, and EUR 0.6m expected loss. Economic capital is EUR 5m. Define pre-tax RAROC=(revenue−costs−EL)/EC. The RAROC is:","choices":["20%","32%","48%","12%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Numérateur ajusté=2,4−0,8−0,6=1,0 M. RAROC=1/5=20 %.","why":["Déduit coûts et EL avant la charge de capital.","Ne déduit pas la perte attendue du revenu ajusté.","Ignore tous les coûts.","Ne correspond pas au numérateur défini."],"cue":"RAROC : préciser le numérateur et le capital.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(2.4-.8-.6)/5","value":19.999999999999996,"optionValue":20,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b071","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-6.1","reading":"CR-6","concept":"Score discrimination versus rating meaning","question":"A retail application score ranks applicants by default risk, while a corporate rating grade is calibrated to a PD range and linked to approval rules. Which statement is most appropriate?","choices":["A score’s numerical scale uniquely determines the rating system’s economic horizon","A single score cutoff implies the same realized loss rate across every segment","Two models with identical rankings must assign identical default probabilities","A good ranking alone does not establish PD calibration or identical economic meaning across rating systems"],"answer":3,"explanation":"L’ordre de risque, la calibration en probabilité et l’usage décisionnel sont des propriétés distinctes.","why":["Le sens d’un score dépend de sa définition et de sa calibration.","PD, LGD et populations peuvent différer.","On peut appliquer différentes calibrations à un même ordre de risque.","Distingue discrimination, calibration et usage."],"cue":"Classer le risque n’est pas encore calibrer une PD.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b072","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-6.2","reading":"CR-6","concept":"PIT deterioration without permanent downgrade","question":"A borrower’s leverage and business model are unchanged, but a severe cyclical downturn weakens next-year repayment capacity. Which rating behavior is more characteristic of a point-in-time system?","choices":["A downgrade only after realized arrears establish a payment default","A grade based solely on the average default rate over a complete historical cycle","A prompt deterioration reflecting current conditions","An unchanged grade designed to look through temporary cyclical weakness"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une notation PIT incorpore davantage les conditions actuelles et leur effet sur la PD à l’horizon retenu.","why":["Le PIT est prospectif et peut réagir avant défaut.","Une moyenne de cycle ne reflète pas seule les conditions courantes.","Correspond à la sensibilité conjoncturelle du PIT.","Décrit davantage une logique TTC."],"cue":"PIT réagit au cycle courant ; TTC cherche davantage à le traverser.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b073","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-6.4","reading":"CR-6","concept":"Issuer versus issue rating","question":"A firm issues senior secured debt and deeply subordinated debt. The issuer’s default likelihood is common, but recoveries differ materially by priority and collateral. Which rating distinction is relevant?","choices":["The common issuer PD implies the two issues must have identical credit ratings","Issue ratings can differ because expected loss and recovery priority differ even for the same issuer","Secured debt cannot have credit risk once its collateral is legally documented","Subordinated debt must have a lower issuer PD because its coupon is typically higher"],"answer":1,"explanation":"La qualité d’une émission intègre ses caractéristiques de priorité et de recouvrement, distinctes du risque de défaut de l’émetteur.","why":["La perte en défaut et la séniorité peuvent modifier la qualité de l’émission.","Identifie la protection propre à la créance.","La valeur et l’exécution du collatéral restent risquées.","Le coupon et le rang ne changent pas mécaniquement la PD de l’émetteur."],"cue":"Même émetteur, pertes différentes selon la créance.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b074","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-7.3","reading":"CR-7","concept":"Retail risk and customer harm","question":"A lender improves short-term collections by repeatedly refinancing distressed customers into larger expensive loans without testing sustainable affordability. Which concern is most direct?","choices":["A higher refinancing balance improves asset quality by reducing current arrears mechanically","Short-term collection performance alone is a sufficient measure of customer outcomes","A new repayment contract is sufficient evidence that affordability has improved","Current arrears reduction may conceal future credit losses and conduct risk"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le refinancement peut reporter les difficultés et aggraver l’endettement, avec risque de crédit et de conduite.","why":["La disparition comptable de l’impayé ne prouve pas une baisse du risque.","Les résultats futurs et la soutenabilité doivent aussi être évalués.","Un contrat ne crée pas de capacité de paiement.","Repère le déplacement du risque et le traitement du client."],"cue":"Une baisse d’impayés peut masquer un report du risque.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b075","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-7.6","reading":"CR-7","concept":"Accuracy ratio from CAP areas","question":"For a default-ranking model, the area under its CAP curve is 0.72, the random-model area is 0.50, and the perfect-model area is 0.95. Using AR=(Amodel−Arandom)/(Aperfect−Arandom), AR is closest to:","choices":["72.0%","22.0%","48.9%","95.0%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"AR=(0,72−0,50)/(0,95−0,50)=0,22/0,45≈48,9 %.","why":["Donne l’aire brute du CAP.","Ne normalise pas l’excès d’aire.","Applique la normalisation fournie.","Donne le benchmark parfait."],"cue":"AR : gain de discrimination relatif au gain parfait.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(.72-.50)/(.95-.50)","value":48.888888888888886,"optionValue":48.9,"tolerance":0.1}},{"id":"b076","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-7.8","reading":"CR-7","concept":"Risk-based pricing and adverse selection","question":"A lender raises APR for risky applicants using historical average PDs, with no allowance for affordability or changes in applicant mix. Which qualification is strongest?","choices":["Historical average PDs can be held fixed because only loan revenue changes with APR","Higher prices can change repayment capacity and borrower selection, so the resulting risk must be reassessed","Pricing by observed risk automatically removes adverse selection and affordability concerns","A higher coupon compensates all additional default risk without a need to re-estimate losses"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le prix peut modifier le comportement, la sélection et l’effort de remboursement ; la relation prix-risque n’est pas statique.","why":["Une intervention de prix peut changer comportement et population.","Identifie la rétroaction de décision.","Le prix peut lui-même affecter sélection et risque.","L’augmentation de revenu promis n’est pas un paiement garanti."],"cue":"Le prix est une intervention qui peut changer le risque.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b077","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-8.1","reading":"CR-8","concept":"Transfer risk despite borrower cash","question":"A solvent importer earns sufficient local currency, but its government blocks conversion and cross-border transfers needed for a USD loan payment. Which source of country risk is most direct?","choices":["Transfer and convertibility restrictions","A loss of collateral priority caused automatically by capital controls","Risk-free duration risk created by the USD denomination","Borrower balance-sheet insolvency established solely by the inability to convert funds"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le paiement extérieur peut échouer malgré les ressources locales en raison de restrictions souveraines de change et transfert.","why":["Cible le blocage souverain décrit.","Aucune modification de la priorité n’est décrite.","Le blocage de transfert n’est pas un choc de taux.","La solvabilité est explicitement distinguée de l’accès aux devises."],"cue":"Ressources locales ne garantissent pas paiement en devise.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b078","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-8.3","reading":"CR-8","concept":"Local-currency sovereign default","question":"An analyst claims that a sovereign can never default on debt denominated in its own currency because it can create money. Which response is best?","choices":["Local-currency debt is default-free unless the sovereign also owes foreign-currency debt","Domestic-currency denomination guarantees payment whenever the sovereign’s tax base is positive","Monetary capacity does not remove political, institutional or economic incentives and constraints that can still lead to local-currency default","Any domestic inflation event is automatically a contractual default on nominal local-currency debt"],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’émission monétaire n’est ni toujours libre institutionnellement ni toujours choisie ; le défaut domestique reste possible.","why":["Un stock de dette étrangère n’est pas une condition nécessaire.","Une base fiscale n’assure pas chaque paiement exigible.","Distingue capacité théorique et décision réelle.","Inflation et manquement contractuel sont des notions distinctes."],"cue":"Pouvoir monétaire ne signifie pas absence de défaut souverain.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b079","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-8.7","reading":"CR-8","concept":"Sovereign CDS as a noisy signal","question":"A sovereign CDS spread widens sharply while its public rating is unchanged. What is the best interpretation?","choices":["The spread may provide a faster market signal, but liquidity and risk premia prevent treating it as a pure physical PD","A market spread and public rating must adjust on the same day to avoid arbitrage","The CDS move is a direct physical PD change once the contract notional is known","The unchanged public rating proves that the CDS move contains no credit information"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les prix de marché réagissent vite mais incorporent des primes et des frictions ; les ratings ont un autre rythme et une autre méthodologie.","why":["Compare vitesse du signal et nature de la mesure.","Les deux objets n’ont pas le même mécanisme d’ajustement.","Le notionnel ne supprime pas les primes de risque et frictions.","Une notation peut réagir plus lentement."],"cue":"Marché rapide ne signifie pas probabilité physique pure.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b080","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-9.2","reading":"CR-9","concept":"Specified Z-score classification","question":"For this exercise, use Z=1.2X1+1.4X2+3.3X3+0.6X4+X5 and classify Z<1.8 as distress, 1.8≤Z≤3.0 as grey, and Z>3.0 as safe. A firm has X=(0.10,0.20,0.08,0.50,1.20). Its result is:","choices":["Z=3.164, safe","Z=1.864, grey","Z=2.164, grey","Z=1.164, distress"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Z=0,12+0,28+0,264+0,30+1,20=2,164. Selon les seuils fournis, le score est dans la zone grise.","why":["Ajoute une unité sans justification.","Omet la contribution de X4.","Pondère toutes les composantes.","Omet un point de chiffre d’affaires relatif."],"cue":"Score composite : formule et seuils doivent être ceux du cas.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"1.2*.1+1.4*.2+3.3*.08+.6*.5+1.2","value":2.1639999999999997,"optionValue":2.164,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b081","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-9.4","reading":"CR-9","concept":"Two-step rating migration","question":"A one-year transition matrix has rows A=(0.80 A,0.18 B,0.02 D), B=(0.10 A,0.80 B,0.10 D), and D=(0,0,1). Assume the same matrix each year. Two-year cumulative default probability starting in A is:","choices":["5.40%","12.00%","2.00%","3.60%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"P(D à deux ans)=0,80×0,02+0,18×0,10+0,02×1=0,054. Inclure les défauts déjà survenus.","why":["Additionne tous les chemins vers défaut.","Additionne des PD de grades sans les poids de migration.","Ne considère qu’une année.","Omet l’état défaut déjà absorbant."],"cue":"Migration : compter les chemins et l’état défaut absorbant.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(.8*.02+.18*.1+.02)","value":5.4,"optionValue":5.4,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b082","topic":"credit","skill":"c-default","objective":"CR-9.6","reading":"CR-9","concept":"Recovery dependence in downturns","question":"A stress model raises borrower PDs but keeps recoveries at benign-year averages even though collateral values fall and many lenders liquidate similar assets. Which concern is most direct?","choices":["The joint stress may understate losses because LGD can rise when defaults rise","Raising PD automatically captures collateral liquidation discounts without changing LGD","Recovery dependency matters only for market risk, not expected credit loss","Keeping recovery fixed is always conservative when more names default"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les mauvaises conditions peuvent simultanément augmenter les défauts et réduire les recouvrements : utiliser une recovery calme sous-estime alors LGD.","why":["Identifie la dépendance défavorable.","Les deux paramètres représentent des mécanismes distincts.","EL dépend de PD et de LGD.","Un recouvrement calme peut être trop optimiste."],"cue":"Stress conjoint : défauts plus fréquents, récupérations possiblement plus faibles.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b083","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-10.1","reading":"CR-10","concept":"Credit VaR horizon and migration","question":"A manager applies a liquid trading-book one-day market VaR process unchanged to a one-year illiquid loan portfolio. Which concern is most important?","choices":["Credit losses have default and migration discontinuities, longer horizons and sparse price data that require a suitable model","One-year loan losses can be inferred exactly from current risk-free duration","Ignoring rating migration is harmless if no borrower has yet defaulted","Scaling a one-day normal VaR linearly to one year fully captures illiquid loan risk"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le crédit comporte des sauts, des migrations, de faibles données de marché et un horizon souvent plus long que le trading quotidien.","why":["Relie le modèle à la structure de perte.","Le défaut et le spread ne sont pas déterminés par la duration sans risque.","Une migration peut changer la valeur et le risque futur.","Le scaling ne crée ni sauts ni états de crédit manquants."],"cue":"Le crédit ne se modélise pas par simple copie de la VaR de marché.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b084","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-10.5","reading":"CR-10","concept":"Migration versus default-only portfolio models","question":"A portfolio contains investment-grade bonds that may lose value materially on downgrade even without default. What is a key reason to use a migration-based model rather than a default-only model?","choices":["It permits recovery risk to be omitted even in default states","It removes the need for a transition matrix by using the current rating alone","It can represent rating-transition-driven changes in value before default","It holds all nondefault bond values fixed while changing only default probability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un modèle de migration valorise les états de notation non défaillants et capture donc des pertes de downgrade.","why":["Le défaut exige toujours une hypothèse de récupération.","Un modèle de migration a besoin de probabilités de transition.","Cible le mécanisme de downgrade.","C’est justement l’omission corrigée par la migration."],"cue":"Migration : perte de valeur dans les états non défaillants.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b085","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-10.6","reading":"CR-10","concept":"Spread-duration loss","question":"A credit bond position is worth EUR 30m and has spread duration 4.2 years. Its spread widens by 80 bp with the risk-free curve unchanged. Ignore convexity and default. Estimated mark-to-market change is:","choices":["EUR −10.08m","EUR +1.008m","EUR −0.1008m","EUR −1.008m"],"answer":3,"explanation":"ΔV≈−V×Dspread×Δs=−30×4,2×0,008=−1,008 M.","why":["Convertit mal les 80 pb.","Inverse le signe d’une hausse de spread.","Divise les points de base par un facteur de trop.","Applique duration de spread et signe négatif."],"cue":"Spread duration : variation décimale et signe de prix.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"-30*4.2*.008","value":-1.008,"optionValue":-1.008,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b086","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-11.1","reading":"CR-11","concept":"Default-indicator correlation","question":"Two default indicators have PDs 5% and 10%, and joint default probability 2%. Using Corr(D1,D2)=[P12−p1p2]/√[p1(1−p1)p2(1−p2)], correlation is closest to:","choices":["0.229","1.000","0.020","0.500"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Numérateur=0,02−0,005=0,015. Dénominateur=√(0,05×0,95×0,10×0,90)≈0,06538 ; corrélation≈0,2294.","why":["Centre puis normalise les indicatrices.","Les défauts ne sont pas parfaitement liés.","Confond probabilité jointe et corrélation.","Utilise un dénominateur inadéquat."],"cue":"Corrélation de défaut : normaliser les indicatrices, pas les actifs.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"(.02-.05*.10)/Math.sqrt(.05*.95*.10*.90)","value":0.22941573387056172,"optionValue":0.229,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b087","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-11.2","reading":"CR-11","concept":"Correlation does not identify the joint law","question":"Two portfolio credit models match all single-name PDs and pairwise default correlations, but produce different extreme portfolio loss probabilities. Which statement is correct?","choices":["A complete pairwise matrix uniquely fixes every joint default state regardless of distribution family","Differences in tail loss must come only from numerical rounding when correlations match","Pairwise correlations do not generally determine all higher-order default dependence","Matching every single-name PD determines the portfolio tail even without a dependence model"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les dépendances d’ordre supérieur et la forme de la loi jointe peuvent différer malgré les mêmes marges et corrélations par paires.","why":["La loi jointe n’est généralement pas identifiée ainsi.","La spécification jointe peut produire des différences économiques réelles.","Identifie l’information manquante d’ordre supérieur.","Les marges seules ne fixent pas les pertes communes."],"cue":"Même matrice de corrélation ne garantit pas même queue de crédit.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b088","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-11.5","reading":"CR-11","concept":"Factor loadings and asset correlation","question":"Asset returns satisfy Xi=βiZ+√(1−βi²)εi, with Z, ε1 and ε2 mutually independent standard normals. If β1=0.6 and β2=0.8, Corr(X1,X2) equals:","choices":["0.48","0.14","1.40","0.70"],"answer":0,"explanation":"La covariance provient seulement du facteur commun : β1β2Var(Z)=0,48. Les variances totales sont unitaires.","why":["Multiplie les deux loadings.","Ne correspond pas au facteur commun.","Additionne les loadings et dépasse le support.","Prend leur moyenne."],"cue":"Facteur standardisé unique : corrélation = produit des loadings.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":".6*.8","value":0.48,"optionValue":0.48,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b089","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-12.1","reading":"CR-12","concept":"Derivative credit risk is replacement risk","question":"A newly entered at-market interest-rate swap has zero market value and no upfront exchange. A trader states that its future counterparty exposure is therefore zero. What is the best correction?","choices":["The notional must be added immediately as an exposure because the initial value is zero","A zero-value trade can create exposure only after the notional is exchanged","Positive future market value is a funding issue and cannot create a counterparty credit claim","Future market moves can create a positive replacement value even when initial value is zero"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une valeur initiale nulle n’empêche pas une valeur positive future, dont la perte au défaut dépend du coût de remplacement.","why":["Le notionnel n’est pas le montant de remplacement.","Le remplacement d’un swap peut être coûteux sans échange de notionnel.","Une valeur positive est bien une créance vulnérable au défaut.","Distingue valeur actuelle et exposition future."],"cue":"Dérivé à zéro aujourd’hui : risque de remplacement demain.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b090","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-12.4","reading":"CR-12","concept":"A guarantee transfers rather than erases risk","question":"A borrower’s loan is fully guaranteed by an affiliated company whose assets depend on the same commodity price. Which assessment is strongest?","choices":["The guarantee can be valued using only the guarantor’s unconditional PD, regardless of its link to the borrower","Common ownership proves the guarantor is a source of independent diversification","A full contractual guarantee permits the lender to ignore guarantor recovery and legal terms","The guarantee requires analysis of enforceability and guarantor dependence, especially under common stress"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le risque est transféré vers un garant dont la capacité peut se dégrader en même temps que celle du débiteur ; la validité juridique compte aussi.","why":["La capacité du garant au moment du défaut est cruciale.","L’affiliation peut renforcer la dépendance.","Une garantie nominale ne garantit pas une exécution intégrale.","Examine capacité conditionnelle et droit."],"cue":"Mitigation : qui paiera précisément dans le scénario de perte ?","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b091","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-12.5","reading":"CR-12","concept":"Structural versus reduced-form dependence","question":"One model derives common defaults from correlated firm-asset values crossing debt barriers. Another makes default intensities respond to a shared economic state. Which classification is appropriate?","choices":["Both require observable default times to be deterministic","Both eliminate systematic risk","The first is structural; the second is reduced-form","The first is reduced-form; the second is structural"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le premier relie défaut et valeur des actifs ; le second modélise directement l’intensité de défaut, avec un facteur commun.","why":["Les deux peuvent être aléatoires.","Le facteur commun crée précisément une dépendance systématique.","Identifie la variable qui génère le défaut.","Inverse les deux constructions."],"cue":"Structurel : actifs/barrière ; reduced-form : intensité de défaut.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b092","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-13.4","reading":"CR-13","concept":"Fixed coupon CDS upfront payment","question":"A CDS has a fixed running coupon of 100 bp, current par spread 160 bp and risky annuity 4.0 years. Ignore accrued premium and convexity. With notional EUR 10m, who pays the approximate upfront amount?","choices":["Protection buyer pays EUR 240,000","No upfront is needed because coupons are fixed","Protection seller pays EUR 240,000","Protection buyer pays EUR 640,000"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le coupon est inférieur au spread de marché. L’acheteur compense par (0,016−0,010)×4×10 M=240 000.","why":["Compense le coupon insuffisant par un paiement initial.","Un coupon standard impose souvent un upfront.","Inverse le sens de compensation.","Valorise tout le spread sans déduire le coupon."],"cue":"Coupon sous le par : l’acheteur paie l’écart en upfront.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"(.016-.010)*4*10000000","value":240000,"optionValue":240000,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b093","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-13.5","reading":"CR-13","concept":"CDS forward versus option commitment","question":"A hedge may be needed six months from now, but management wants the right to buy protection then without an obligation to enter the CDS if spreads tighten. Which instrument fits best?","choices":["An immediate sale of protection with the same expiry as the future hedge need","A CDS forward under which management can abandon the trade without compensation","An option to buy CDS protection, with terms and default treatment specified","A mandatory forward-starting CDS at a fixed spread with no cancellation right"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une option de protection confère un droit d’entrée futur ; un forward impose l’échange selon ses termes. Le traitement d’un défaut préalable doit être précisé.","why":["Vendre protection prend le risque opposé.","Une faculté gratuite d’abandon serait une optionalité distincte à définir et valoriser.","Correspond au droit asymétrique souhaité.","Le forward impose une obligation."],"cue":"Forward : engagement ; option : droit, avec prime et clauses.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b094","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-13.7","reading":"CR-13","concept":"Base versus compound correlation","question":"A dealer quotes an implied correlation separately for a 3–7% tranche and base correlations for 0–3% and 0–7% equity tranches. Which description is correct?","choices":["Compound correlation is obtained by subtracting two base-correlation numbers without repricing tranches","Base correlation is the single physical asset correlation shared by all detachment points","The two quoted conventions must give identical implied correlation at every attachment","Compound correlation fits the quoted tranche directly; base correlations fit equity tranches used to construct the tranche value difference"],"answer":3,"explanation":"La corrélation compound reproduit une tranche donnée ; la base correlation porte sur les tranches partant de zéro, dont les valeurs peuvent être différenciées.","why":["On différencie des valeurs de tranches, pas simplement des corrélations.","La base correlation est implicite aux prix et peut varier.","Les conventions calibrent des objets différents.","Distingue les objets calibrés."],"cue":"Corrélation implicite : identifier la tranche calibrée.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b095","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-14.3","reading":"CR-14","concept":"Clearing transforms legal counterparties","question":"A bilateral swap is accepted for central clearing and legally novated. What happens to the original bilateral counterparty relationship?","choices":["The original bilateral contract survives with the CCP as only an administrative valuation agent","Only trade reporting changes; the original bilateral legal claims are necessarily unchanged","It is replaced by contracts with the CCP under the clearing framework","Novation removes the market exposure along with the old counterparty relationship"],"answer":2,"explanation":"La novation substitue la CCP dans la relation contractuelle, sans supprimer l’exposition économique de taux ni les exigences de marge.","why":["La CCP devient contrepartie selon le dispositif, pas simple agent.","Le cas précise une novation juridique.","Décrit le changement juridique.","La position économique peut être maintenue."],"cue":"Clearing : changer la contrepartie, pas supprimer le marché.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b096","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-14.8","reading":"CR-14","concept":"Variation margin versus initial margin","question":"A cleared derivative has a current mark-to-market loss of EUR 2m. Additional potential adverse moves during close-out are modeled separately. Which allocation of margin purposes is correct?","choices":["Variation margin covers current value changes; initial margin targets potential changes during close-out","Initial margin pays every daily mark-to-market while variation margin covers only remote stress","Neither margin addresses counterparty exposure","The two amounts are interchangeable accounting labels"],"answer":0,"explanation":"VM règle les variations courantes ; IM protège contre la variation potentielle entre le dernier échange et la liquidation après défaut.","why":["Aligne chaque marge sur son horizon.","Inverse les fonctions usuelles.","Elles servent à réduire l’exposition de crédit.","Les finalités et conditions de restitution diffèrent."],"cue":"VM : valeur courante ; IM : risque pendant liquidation.","source":"https://www.bis.org/cpmi/publ/d101a.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b097","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-14.9","reading":"CR-14","concept":"SPV limitations in risk mitigation","question":"A bank transfers exposures to a bankruptcy-remote SPV but retains a liquidity facility that can be drawn during asset stress. What should risk management conclude?","choices":["The liquidity facility can be ignored if it has never previously been drawn","A transfer of legal ownership guarantees that asset stress cannot affect the originating bank","Bankruptcy remoteness makes the retained liquidity facility default-free","Legal separation does not remove retained contingent exposures or every economic linkage"],"answer":3,"explanation":"La séparation juridique peut être utile, mais la ligne conservée recrée une exposition conditionnelle, souvent activée en stress.","why":["Un engagement non utilisé reste un engagement.","Le soutien retenu rétablit un lien économique.","Le risque de tirage et de remboursement reste à analyser.","Identifie l’exposition conservée."],"cue":"SPV : vérifier les liens et soutiens qui restent.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b098","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-15.1","reading":"CR-15","concept":"Counterparty versus loan exposure uncertainty","question":"Compare a EUR 20m fixed loan with an uncollateralized swap of EUR 20m notional. Which distinction is most important?","choices":["Equal notionals imply equal current positive exposure and identical future exposure distributions","A negative current swap value ensures that the bank can never become exposed later","The swap’s future positive replacement exposure can vary with market conditions, while loan principal exposure is usually more directly specified","The loan has recovery uncertainty, whereas derivatives cannot have recovery uncertainty"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le dérivé peut avoir une valeur future positive ou négative ; son notionnel ne détermine pas directement la perte de remplacement.","why":["Le notionnel ne détermine pas la valeur de remplacement.","Le mark-to-market peut changer de signe.","Identifie la valeur aléatoire du dérivé.","La récupération compte aussi pour les dérivés."],"cue":"Prêt : principal ; dérivé : valeur de remplacement future.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b099","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-15.5","reading":"CR-15","concept":"CVA price versus credit limits","question":"A desk charges a model-based CVA on a large uncollateralized derivative with a weak counterparty. It asks to waive all credit limits because the risk has been priced. Which response is strongest?","choices":["A price adjustment does not eliminate default loss, concentration or model risk, so limits remain relevant","Positive expected trade revenue is sufficient to waive concentration limits","A charged CVA is economically equivalent to receiving segregated collateral of the full potential loss","The CVA charge converts a risky derivative into a default-free exposure once booked"],"answer":0,"explanation":"CVA valorise une perte attendue et ses hypothèses ; elle ne constitue pas une protection qui empêche les pertes extrêmes ou la concentration.","why":["Sépare tarification et maîtrise du risque.","La rémunération et la concentration doivent être évaluées séparément.","Un ajustement de prix ne constitue pas une garantie.","Le contrat reste exposé au défaut."],"cue":"CVA rémunère un risque ; une limite le borne.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b100","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-15.8","reading":"CR-15","concept":"Avoiding xVA double counting","question":"A bank adds funding, collateral and counterparty adjustments to a clean derivative price. A reviewer finds the same collateral funding cash flow charged in both FVA and another adjustment. What is the right response?","choices":["Reconcile cash-flow definitions and valuation conventions to remove double counting","Keep both charges because differently named adjustments cannot overlap","Select the adjustment with the more conservative label without examining its cash flows","Remove the clean price and add every xVA to avoid inconsistent discounting"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les ajustements dépendent de conventions cohérentes et de cashflows parfois liés ; leurs noms ne garantissent pas l’additivité sans recouvrement.","why":["Cible le chevauchement économique.","Les noms ne garantissent pas l’indépendance.","Une étiquette ne remplace pas la réconciliation.","Cela ne résout pas le recouvrement des cashflows."],"cue":"xVA : réconcilier les cashflows avant d’additionner les étiquettes.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b101","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-16.2","reading":"CR-16","concept":"Netting requires the right legal set","question":"A dealer has +9m and −7m replacement values against two subsidiaries in the same corporate group. There is no enforceable cross-entity netting agreement. Which current positive exposure is appropriate before collateral?","choices":["EUR 9m","EUR 0m","EUR 2m","EUR 16m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sans netting juridiquement valable entre entités, le +9 M reste une créance exposée ; le −7 M ne peut pas la compenser.","why":["Respecte les ensembles de netting distincts.","Suppose une compensation non autorisée.","Nette deux personnes juridiques sans droit.","Additionne la dette du dealer à son exposition positive."],"cue":"Netting : vérifier la personne juridique et l’opposabilité.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"Math.max(9,0)+Math.max(-7,0)","value":9,"optionValue":9,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b102","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-16.4","reading":"CR-16","concept":"Compression without market-risk change","question":"A dealer tears up offsetting swaps and replaces them with fewer contracts designed to preserve aggregate cash flows and market sensitivities. What is the primary compression benefit?","choices":["The reduced contract count guarantees that every close-out and legal risk is eliminated","Equal net market exposure implies equal legal counterparty exposure before and after compression","Lower gross notional and operational burden without necessarily changing net market exposure","Compression removes replacement-cost risk even if the remaining contracts are unsecured"],"answer":2,"explanation":"La compression réduit des contrats redondants et les montants bruts, tout en cherchant à préserver le risque économique net.","why":["Une simplification ne garantit pas l’élimination des risques résiduels.","Les ensembles et caractéristiques contractuelles peuvent changer l’exposition de crédit.","Décrit le bénéfice recherché.","Un solde non garanti peut conserver une exposition."],"cue":"Compression : simplifier le brut en préservant le net.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b103","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-16.5","reading":"CR-16","concept":"Bilateral swap compression balance","question":"For the same counterparty, maturity and fixed rate, a dealer has three swaps: pay-fixed EUR 70m, receive-fixed EUR 45m, and receive-fixed EUR 10m. Assuming exact cash-flow offset and full compression, the remaining position is:","choices":["No remaining position","Pay-fixed EUR 125m","Receive-fixed EUR 15m","Pay-fixed EUR 15m"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Position nette payeuse=70−45−10=15 M. Les deux sens ne s’annulent pas complètement.","why":["Omet le solde résiduel.","Additionne les notionnels bruts.","Inverse le signe.","Conserve le signe de la position nette."],"cue":"Compression : signer les flux avant d’additionner.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"70-45-10","value":15,"optionValue":15,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b104","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-17.4","reading":"CR-17","concept":"Valuation-agent dispute control","question":"A counterparty acting as valuation agent demands a large margin call. Independent prices imply a materially smaller amount. What is the strongest operational response?","choices":["Accept the full amount without review because the valuation agent’s role eliminates contractual dispute rights","Use the lower valuation automatically because it minimizes the bank’s immediate funding cost","Withhold all current and future margin on every contract until the disputed trade matures","Follow agreed dispute procedures, exchange undisputed collateral where required, and reconcile valuations using independent inputs"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le rôle d’agent n’élimine pas les litiges ; il faut respecter le contrat et rapprocher les données et méthodes de manière traçable.","why":["Le contrat peut définir des droits de contestation.","Le coût de financement ne décide pas de la valeur correcte.","La réponse doit respecter les obligations applicables, dont les montants non contestés.","Combine contrôle et processus contractuel."],"cue":"Agent de valorisation : autorité définie, contrôle et contestation possibles.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b105","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-17.6","reading":"CR-17","concept":"Diagnosing repeated collateral breaks","question":"Two firms disagree daily on swap collateral although their trade inventories match. One uses yesterday’s curve and the other today’s curve. Which action targets the root cause?","choices":["Align valuation dates and market-data conventions before escalating the residual pricing dispute","Net the disputed amount against an unrelated legal entity to avoid resolving the break","Raise the minimum transfer amount as the primary cure for the different valuation dates","Assume matched trade inventories imply that one valuation agent is acting in bad faith"],"answer":0,"explanation":"L’inventaire commun ne suffit pas si les valorisations reposent sur des dates de marché différentes.","why":["Corrige la cause de convention.","Le netting suppose une base juridique appropriée et ne répare pas le prix.","Un seuil plus élevé masque le problème.","Les dates différentes expliquent déjà une divergence possible."],"cue":"Rapprocher trades, dates, prix et méthodes séparément.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b106","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-17.9","reading":"CR-17","concept":"Segregation and funding availability","question":"A dealer receives EUR 12m of initial margin that is legally segregated and cannot be rehypothecated. Treasury wants to count it as cash available for unrelated margin payments. What is correct?","choices":["Credit protection and treasury liquidity must be identical because both are measured in euros","Treasury can count the cash as free funding provided it also records an equal collateral liability","The collateral can protect against counterparty loss but is not freely available treasury funding under these terms","Legal ownership of a collateral claim is sufficient to establish unrestricted reuse rights"],"answer":2,"explanation":"La ségrégation peut protéger la garantie, mais les restrictions d’usage empêchent de la compter comme liquidité libre.","why":["Les mécanismes et disponibilités diffèrent.","Une écriture comptable ne supprime pas la restriction juridique.","Distingue protection de crédit et droit d’usage.","Les restrictions d’usage sont déterminantes."],"cue":"Garantie reçue n’est pas forcément liquidité réutilisable.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b107","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-18.2","reading":"CR-18","concept":"Novation does not eliminate CCP dependence","question":"After novation, a clearing member states that bilateral default risk has vanished so counterparty risk need no longer be monitored. Which correction is best?","choices":["Replacing the original counterparty means that no default exposure remains to any institution","The legal counterparty changes to the CCP and clearing framework, creating a different exposure and dependence structure","Central clearing prevents liquidity stress even if many members face simultaneous margin calls","The member’s initial margin can be treated as an unconditional guarantee of every CCP obligation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"La centralisation transforme la structure de risque et la concentre vers la CCP ; elle ne l’annule pas.","why":["Le risque devient notamment une exposition vers la structure de clearing.","Identifie le transfert de risque.","Des appels de marge simultanés peuvent créer un fort besoin de liquidité.","La marge n’est pas une garantie illimitée des engagements de la CCP."],"cue":"Novation : transfert de contrepartie, pas absence de risque.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b108","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-18.6","reading":"CR-18","concept":"Specified CCP waterfall arithmetic","question":"A CCP faces a defaulting member’s EUR 90m close-out loss. The stated waterfall uses that member’s IM of 55m, its default-fund contribution of 10m, then CCP capital of 5m, before mutualized resources. How much reaches mutualized resources?","choices":["EUR 35m","EUR 20m","EUR 30m","EUR 25m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Perte résiduelle=90−55−10−5=20 M. L’ordre et les ressources sont ceux explicitement stipulés dans le cas.","why":["Ne déduit que l’IM.","Déduit les trois premières couches.","Omet une autre couche.","Omet le capital CCP."],"cue":"Waterfall : suivre l’ordre contractuel sans sauter de couche.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"Math.max(90-55-10-5,0)","value":20,"optionValue":20,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b109","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-18.9","reading":"CR-18","concept":"Initial margin and default-fund incentives","question":"A CCP proposal lowers every member’s own initial margin and shifts the same modeled protection into a shared default fund. Which concern deserves attention?","choices":["Mutualizing a member’s risk always makes its own marginal cost of risk-taking higher","A larger shared fund makes risk-based initial margin unnecessary regardless of member portfolios","More mutualization can shift a member’s risk costs toward others and weaken incentives unless the framework addresses moral hazard","Equal total modeled protection implies identical incentives under every allocation between IM and default funds"],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’IM est d’abord une ressource du membre qui fait défaut ; une mutualisation accrue peut externaliser une partie du coût de sa prise de risque.","why":["Transférer une partie du coût vers les autres peut faire l’inverse.","Les risques individuels et leurs coûts doivent encore être contrôlés.","Relie mutualisation et incitations.","La répartition de la perte conditionnelle change les incitations."],"cue":"Defaulter-pays et mutualisation n’ont pas les mêmes incitations.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b110","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-19.4","reading":"CR-19","concept":"Option premium timing and exposure profile","question":"A bank buys a European option and pays its premium upfront. Before expiry the option can have positive value to the bank; after expiry all obligations settle immediately. Which exposure profile is most consistent?","choices":["Positive potential exposure before expiry that falls to zero after final settlement","Zero exposure until exercise because paying the premium removes the seller’s contingent obligation","Exposure equal to the option notional until one year after final settlement","Exposure equal to the initial premium at every future date regardless of spot changes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le paiement de prime n’efface pas la valeur de remplacement positive de l’option achetée ; le risque prend fin après règlement intégral.","why":["Respecte la valeur du droit et la fin de la créance.","Le vendeur reste engagé envers la valeur positive de l’option.","Ni le notionnel ni ce délai supplémentaire ne sont justifiés.","La valeur du droit varie avec le marché et le temps."],"cue":"Option achetée : prime payée, mais créance future toujours possible.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b111","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-19.5","reading":"CR-19","concept":"Coupon settlement and exposure sawtooth","question":"A swap’s positive value includes a large accrued coupon due tomorrow. All else equal, immediately after that coupon is paid, what happens to the exposure attributable to that coupon?","choices":["It falls because the accrued receivable has been settled","It rises by the coupon amount because a successful payment raises the remaining contractual receivable","It remains unchanged because payment timing cannot affect an exposure profile","It falls to zero for the whole swap regardless of its remaining cash flows"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Un flux reçu cesse d’être une créance future. Les autres flux et mouvements de marché continuent de déterminer l’exposition résiduelle.","why":["Le coupon payé cesse d’être une créance.","Le paiement réduit le montant restant dû sur ce flux.","Les règlements modifient bien les créances restantes.","Les autres flux peuvent conserver une valeur de remplacement."],"cue":"Profil d’exposition : localiser les paiements, pas seulement l’échéance finale.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b112","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-19.7","reading":"CR-19","concept":"Credit protection versus funding need","question":"A fully margined dealer must post cash collateral as market values move against it. Its credit exposure to the counterparty is small, but collateral calls are large. Which conclusion is best?","choices":["A margin agreement can be judged only by its credit-risk reduction, without considering cash-call timing","A fully margined position has no treasury cash requirement once initial margin has been posted","Funding exposure is always the positive part of the same unsecured credit exposure measure","Low unsecured credit exposure can coexist with material funding liquidity exposure"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le collatéral réduit certaines pertes de contrepartie tout en exigeant des liquidités du débiteur de marge.","why":["Les dates et conditions de financement sont importantes.","Les VM et autres appels peuvent générer du cash à fournir.","Les définitions, signes et horizons peuvent différer.","Distingue deux mécanismes."],"cue":"Moins de risque de crédit peut signifier plus de besoin de financement.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b113","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-20.4","reading":"CR-20","concept":"Recovery sensitivity holding hazard fixed","question":"For a one-period uncollateralized exposure, assume fixed EE=EUR 20m, fixed default probability 3%, and discount factor 1. Recovery falls from 40% to 25%, while PD stays fixed. The increase in unilateral CVA is:","choices":["EUR 0.090m","EUR 0.150m","EUR 0.450m","EUR 0.030m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔCVA=20×0,03×[(1−0,25)−(1−0,40)]=0,09 M. Ici la PD est explicitement maintenue constante.","why":["Applique seulement l’augmentation de LGD.","Confond points de recovery et perte en montant.","Donne la nouvelle CVA totale.","Utilise un montant d’exposition trop faible."],"cue":"Sensibilité recovery : préciser ce qui reste constant.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"20*.03*((1-.25)-(1-.40))","value":0.09000000000000001,"optionValue":0.09,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b114","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-20.7","reading":"CR-20","concept":"Bilateral value-adjustment sign","question":"Under the stated convention, risky derivative value equals clean value minus unilateral CVA plus unilateral DVA. Clean value is EUR 18m, CVA EUR 1.2m, and DVA EUR 0.5m. The risky value is:","choices":["EUR 18.7m","EUR 16.8m","EUR 16.3m","EUR 17.3m"],"answer":3,"explanation":"V=18−1,2+0,5=17,3 M. La déduction bilatérale nette est 0,7 M selon cette convention.","why":["Ajoute le solde au lieu de le soustraire.","Soustrait CVA mais omet le bénéfice DVA prévu par la convention.","Soustrait aussi DVA.","Respecte la convention de signes donnée."],"cue":"CVA et DVA : écrire d’abord la convention de valeur.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"18-1.2+.5","value":17.3,"optionValue":17.3,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b115","topic":"credit","skill":"c-price","objective":"CR-20.9","reading":"CR-20","concept":"Incremental CVA from a new trade","question":"A netting set has CVA EUR 1.0m before a new trade and EUR 1.3m afterward. The new trade’s standalone CVA is EUR 0.5m. What CVA cost is incremental to this portfolio?","choices":["EUR 0.5m","EUR 1.8m","EUR 0.3m","EUR 0.2m"],"answer":2,"explanation":"CVA incrémentale=1,3−1,0=0,3 M. La CVA standalone ne tient pas compte des interactions dans le netting set.","why":["Ignore le portefeuille existant.","Additionne des valeurs incompatibles.","Prend la différence avec et sans la transaction.","Calcule le bénéfice de netting relatif au standalone."],"cue":"Incrémental = portefeuille avec moins portefeuille sans.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"1.3-1","value":0.30000000000000004,"optionValue":0.3,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b116","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-21.4","reading":"CR-21","concept":"Stress loss relative to baseline EL","question":"A loan portfolio has EAD EUR 200m. Baseline PD=2%, LGD=40%; stress PD=7%, LGD=55%. Define stress loss here as stressed expected loss minus baseline expected loss. The stress loss is:","choices":["EUR 9.3m","EUR 7.7m","EUR 6.1m","EUR 1.6m"],"answer":2,"explanation":"ELbase=200×0,02×0,40=1,6. ELstress=200×0,07×0,55=7,7. Différence=6,1 M.","why":["Additionne base et stress.","Donne le niveau stressé sans déduire la base.","Utilise la convention de différence précisée.","Donne EL de base."],"cue":"Stress : distinguer niveau stressé et perte incrémentale.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"200*.07*.55-200*.02*.4","value":6.100000000000001,"optionValue":6.1,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b117","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-21.6","reading":"CR-21","concept":"Joint exposure and PD stress in CVA","question":"A simplified one-period CVA uses EE×PD×LGD with no discounting. Baseline EE=EUR 10m, PD=2%, LGD=60%; stress EE=EUR 16m and PD=5%, same LGD. Incremental CVA stress loss is:","choices":["EUR 0.30m","EUR 0.36m","EUR 0.12m","EUR 0.48m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"CVA base=10×0,02×0,60=0,12. Stress=16×0,05×0,60=0,48. Hausse=0,36 M.","why":["Modifie seulement PD sur l’ancienne exposition.","Stresse conjointement exposition et défaut puis retranche la base.","Donne la base.","Donne le niveau stressé, pas la hausse."],"cue":"CVA stress : cohérence des expositions, PD et comparaison de base.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"16*.05*.6-10*.02*.6","value":0.36,"optionValue":0.36,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b118","topic":"credit","skill":"c-exposure","objective":"CR-21.8","reading":"CR-21","concept":"Inconsistent counterparty stress scenarios","question":"A stress report increases counterparty PD under recession but keeps exposures at values from a benign scenario, despite trades losing their hedge when the same commodity price falls. Which pitfall is present?","choices":["Recession scenarios should exclude market-factor shocks to avoid counting the same stress twice","Using a stressed PD automatically transforms the benign exposure into conditional stressed exposure","Updating only PD is sufficient as long as the unchanged exposure is an unconditional average","Inconsistent scenario application can miss joint exposure-default deterioration"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le scénario doit relier les facteurs de marché et la qualité de crédit ; sinon il peut manquer le wrong-way risk et la rupture du hedge.","why":["Les facteurs doivent être cohérents, pas omis arbitrairement.","Multiplier par une nouvelle PD ne change pas la distribution d’exposition.","La dépendance et les effets conditionnels peuvent être essentiels.","Identifie l’incohérence économique."],"cue":"Stress CCR : même monde économique pour exposition et défaut.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b119","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-22.4","reading":"CR-22","concept":"Originate-to-distribute incentive","question":"An originator sells most loan credit risk into a securitization and is paid mainly on issuance volume. Investors lack granular underwriting data. Which conflict is most important?","choices":["The originator may weaken screening when it does not bear much of the resulting credit loss","Volume-based fees necessarily align underwriting quality with investors’ long-run losses","A sold loan’s initial underwriting is irrelevant once a waterfall ranks the investors","Investors can rely solely on the originator’s retained servicing role as proof of full risk alignment"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le transfert de risque et une rémunération au volume peuvent détacher l’intérêt de l’originateur de la qualité future des prêts.","why":["Identifie l’incitation à sélectionner moins rigoureusement.","La rémunération au volume peut créer le conflit contraire.","La waterfall répartit les pertes sans réparer les actifs faibles.","Le servicing ne garantit pas une exposition économique suffisante."],"cue":"Securitisation : suivre qui choisit le risque et qui supporte la perte.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b120","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-22.5","reading":"CR-22","concept":"Specified interest waterfall","question":"A securitization receives EUR 8m interest cash this period. Pay servicing 1m, senior interest 4m, then mezzanine interest due 2m, with any residual to equity. No trigger is breached and no principal cash is available. Equity receives:","choices":["EUR 3m","EUR 2m","EUR 0m","EUR 1m"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Cash résiduel=8−1−4−2=1 M. Toutes les couches prioritaires sont servies avant equity.","why":["Ne paie pas l’intérêt mezzanine.","Omet une partie des paiements prioritaires.","Suppose une absence de résidu.","Applique la cascade explicitement donnée."],"cue":"Waterfall : déduire chaque rang avant l’equity.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"Math.max(8-1-4-2,0)","value":1,"optionValue":1,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b121","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-22.6","reading":"CR-22","concept":"Excess-spread reserve replenishment","question":"A reserve starts the year at EUR 3m. Credit losses of 2m are charged to it. Available excess spread of 4m then replenishes the reserve up to a target of 4m; the remainder goes to equity. End-year reserve and equity distribution are:","choices":["EUR 3m and EUR 2m","EUR 4m and EUR 1m","EUR 1m and EUR 4m","EUR 5m and EUR 0m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Après pertes, réserve=1 M. Il faut 3 M pour atteindre la cible de 4 ; le dernier million d’excess spread va à equity.","why":["Conserve à tort l’ancienne cible de 3.","Reconstitue la réserve puis distribue l’excédent.","Omet l’affectation prioritaire à la réserve.","Ignore le plafond de réserve."],"cue":"Excess spread : pertes, reconstitution ciblée, puis distribution.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"Math.max(4-(4-(3-2)),0)","value":1,"optionValue":1,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b122","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-23.3","reading":"CR-23","concept":"Revolving versus amortizing structures","question":"Credit-card receivables repay rapidly, but a securitization is designed to maintain an asset pool during an initial revolving period. Which mechanism is most relevant?","choices":["Use eligible principal collections to purchase new receivables during the permitted revolving period","Maintain the pool by treating finance-charge income as newly created principal receivables","Keep adding new receivables without any eligibility or early-amortization conditions","Use every principal collection immediately to amortize all notes while keeping the original pool size unchanged"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Une structure revolving réinvestit les collections de principal pendant une période autorisée, sous conditions de qualité et de triggers.","why":["Décrit le mécanisme de réinvestissement.","Le revenu ne remplace pas automatiquement une créance principale.","Les conditions de qualité et les triggers protègent la structure.","Amortir sans remplacement fait décroître les actifs."],"cue":"Revolving : réinvestir sous règles, puis amortir selon les triggers.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b123","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-23.7","reading":"CR-23","concept":"WAL from principal repayment timing","question":"A securitized note repays principal of EUR 20m at year 1, EUR 30m at year 2, and EUR 50m at year 4. Interest is excluded. The weighted average life is:","choices":["3.0 years","4.0 years","2.0 years","2.8 years"],"answer":3,"explanation":"WAL=(20×1+30×2+50×4)/(20+30+50)=280/100=2,8 ans.","why":["Utilise une pondération incorrecte.","Ne retient que la dernière échéance.","Ignore la taille des flux tardifs.","Pondère chaque remboursement de principal par sa date."],"cue":"WAL : moyenne des dates pondérée par le principal.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"(20*1+30*2+50*4)/(20+30+50)","value":2.8,"optionValue":2.8,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b124","topic":"credit","skill":"c-pool","objective":"CR-23.8","reading":"CR-23","concept":"Monthly prepayment to annual CPR","question":"A mortgage pool has a constant single-month mortality rate SMM=1%. Ignore scheduled amortization in this conversion. CPR=1−(1−SMM)^12 is closest to:","choices":["12.00%","88.64%","1.00%","11.36%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"CPR=1−0,99^12≈0,113615=11,36 %. La conversion tient compte des prêts déjà remboursés les mois précédents.","why":["Additionne linéairement les taux mensuels.","Donne la survie, pas le prépaiement.","Conserve le taux mensuel.","Compose la survie mensuelle sur un an."],"cue":"CPR = 1 moins la survie mensuelle composée.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(1-(1-.01)**12)","value":11.361512828387077,"optionValue":11.36,"tolerance":0.01}}];
